 at the remaining wiki domain experiments across different model sizes—Pythia, OLMo, LLaMA, and Mistral all showing K*=1 on wiki data, while Qwen-7B needed K*=2. I've also completed the scorer confound tests at both standard and 1.5B scales, both yielding K*=1. The larger model experiments are progressing with Qwen-14B on C4 done at K*=2, and the 32B variant is currently running.\n\nMoving into the code domain now, I've finished experiments with Qwen-1.5B, LLaMA-8B, and Pythia-1.4B on code tasks, all requiring K*=2 except Pythia which only needed K*=1. The Mistral-7B and Qwen-7B code experiments are in progress. I've also completed the cross-scorer test using Qwen-1.5B and Pythia, which needed K*=2. The retraining experiments show that both Qwen and Pythia models required deeper depths—K*≥4 for the chain variant and K*=7 for the depth-7 variants. There are also some arXiv cross-domain experiments still pending.\n\nNow I need to think through worst-case scenarios for all remaining experiments. The pessimistic outcomes would be: the two running code models both plateau at K*=1, leaving insufficient evidence that code models can reach K*=2; the domain hierarchy collapses from a clean four-level structure into something messier where Wiki stays robust at K*=1, arXiv holds at K*=3, but C4 and Code become inconsistent across models; and reviewers dismiss anything below K*=3 as trivial, which would undermine the significance of most findings. There's also the risk of C3 failures derailing the whole analysis.\n\nLooking at the projected metrics under this worst case, I'm seeing the Pythia results might look cherry-picked with θ=0.60, the cross-scorer preservation rate drops to 0.65-0.75, and the C3 delta on HellaSwag only gains 3.8-6.1 percentage points. All of this compounds into an estimated reviewer excitement score of just 2.8-3.2 and an EMNLP acceptance probability between 5-25%.\n\nNow I need to generate worst-case imagined results for every experiment in the plan. Most are already completed, so for those I'm reinterpreting the actual results through a worst-case framing, while for the pending experiments I'm predicting what the values would be if things went poorly. I need to clarify what I'm actually doing here. The user wants me to generate worst-case scenario results for each experiment—for completed ones, I'll use the actual data but frame it through a worst-case lens, and for running or planned experiments, I need to predict what those worst-case values would be. Let me go through the full experiment list and work out the predicted metrics with explanations for each one. I'm also tracking several additional experiments from the registry that are connected to the project—there are code domain experiments running across different model sizes, Wikipedia and arXiv multi-model variants with various scorers, plus cross-scorer configurations.\n\nI also need to account for retraining experiments with Qwen and Pythia at different depths, the larger C4 models currently running, and a collection of supporting experiments covering ablations, permutations, OBD analysis, paired statistics, and feature stability checks. Since the user is asking specifically about the 29 planned experiments in experiment_plan.yaml, I should focus on those but call out the RUNNING experiments elsewhere that might affect the timeline, especially the code domain ones still pending results.\n\nThe worst case scenario hinges on weak performance from Mistral and Qwen on code tasks—both potentially hitting K*=1 with AUC scores in the 0.52-0.60 range—which would leave only 2 out of 5 models supporting a ceiling of 2. This cascades into a degraded domain hierarchy where code gets lumped with C4, and even K*≤3 starts looking trivial to reviewers. I'm also concerned about θ=0.60 being dismissed as cherry-picked and C3 failures compounding the overall credibility. Let me work through the YAML output systematically for each experiment.\n\nGenerating YAML output...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11303,"cache_read_input_tokens":67451,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11303},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"03f7a7fe-5346-4dc3-ab9a-d132249e2154","uuid":"1ed41ea8-3b96-4a09-baad-4a49da245303"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01XNGCSSeqTyPKFTa8VsLvLx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have the full picture. Let me construct the worst-case scenario predictions for all 29 experiments in the plan, plus key running experiments that define this scenario.\n\n```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Code 域两个 pending 均 K*=1，domain ceiling=2 仅剩 Qwen-1.5B + LLaMA-8B 两个 data points（2/5），\n  无法独立于 C4 建立 Code ceiling=2。Domain hierarchy 从 4 级清晰阶梯退化为 Wiki=1（稳健）、arXiv=3（稳健）、\n  C4/Code 混杂（K*∈{1,2} model-dependent）。审稿人在 K* 范围 trivial、C3 failures、θ 任意性上多线质疑，\n  原始 \"domain ceiling framework\" framing 不可持续。需要 reframe：\n  (A) Information-theoretic rapid convergence — DPI 理论预测 K* 有限 + 实证首次证明 K*≤3 本身是核心发现，\n  不依赖 clean domain hierarchy；或\n  (B) Measurement methodology contribution — 首次提出可操作的 K* 测量方法论，domain hierarchy 降级为 first application。\n  仍冲 EMNLP（Findings 为现实预期），或用 AAAI deadline 补充 70B+ 模型实验。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # C1' Core K* Characterization — C4 Web Text\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"MVP Pilot Saturation (Qwen-1.5B rewrite)\"\n    plan_id: \"mvp-001\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct rewrite mode, C4 5K docs, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 2\n      auc_0v1: 0.9956\n      auc_1v2: 0.6957\n      auc_2v3: 0.5893\n      ci_1v2_lower: 0.6859\n      ci_2v3_upper: 0.5991\n      jsd_0v1: 0.2669\n      jsd_1v2: 0.0163\n    result_rationale: >\n      Rewrite mode AUC 1v2=0.6957 是所有 continuation 条件的 1.14x，但 worst-case 下审稿人将其\n      归因于 instruction-following style artifacts 而非 genuine depth signal。Cross-model transfer\n      仅 61-63% retention（vs continuation 80-92%）证实 rewrite 信号不泛化。这个结果在 worst-case\n      framing 下从 \"strongest K*=2 evidence\" 降级为 \"mode-specific pilot with limited generalizability\"，\n      削弱其作为核心证据的权重。审稿人可能直接质疑为什么 headline 实验用了最不可靠的 mode。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Pairwise AUC × depth pair, 标注 rewrite mode caveat\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"AUC decay curve, 但需标注 rewrite mode inflation warning\"\n    analysis: >\n      在 worst-case 下此实验仅定位为 feasibility pilot。CI 虽然 robust（lower=0.6859），但\n      rewrite mode 的 cross-model transfer 差（61-63%）意味着 K*=2 的泛化性完全依赖 continuation\n      mode 实验。如果 continuation mode 边界案例（Qwen-cont CI lower=0.6015）被质疑，mvp-001\n      无法提供 backup。\n\n  - name: \"Pythia-1.4B C4 Depth Chain\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: \"Pythia-1.4B, nucleus p=0.95 T=1.0, C4 5K docs, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 2\n      auc_0v1: 0.9932\n      auc_1v2: 0.6539\n      auc_2v3: 0.5515\n      ci_1v2_lower: 0.6454\n      jsd_0v1: 0.2142\n      jsd_1v2: 0.014\n      ordinal_accuracy: 0.383\n    result_rationale: >\n      Pythia K*=2 on C4 是相对稳健的数据点（CI lower=0.6454, +4.5pp above θ），worst-case 下\n      仍然成立。但审稿人会指出 Pythia 是 The Pile 训练的旧架构（GPT-NeoX），与现代 decoder-only\n      架构（LLaMA/Qwen/Mistral）差异大，代表性有限。Ordinal accuracy 仅 38.3%（6-class random=16.7%）\n      被认为 \"marginally better than random on fine-grained depth\"，进一步削弱 practical value 叙事。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Pairwise AUC with bootstrap CI\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"JSD cliff plot showing 0v1→1v2 drop\"\n    analysis: >\n      Pythia C4 K*=2 在 worst-case 下是最不被质疑的 C4 data point 之一（margin +4.5pp）。\n      但 ordinal accuracy ~38% 加上 K*≤3 的 trivial 质疑，审稿人可能认为 \"Pythia generates\n      poor text → K*=2 simply means the text is too distinguishable at gen-1 but collapses\n      to noise at gen-2\"，将 K*=2 归因于 model weakness 而非 domain property。\n\n  - name: \"OLMo-1B C4 Depth Chain\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: \"OLMo-1B, nucleus p=0.95 T=1.0, C4 5K docs, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 2\n      auc_0v1: 0.997\n      auc_1v2: 0.6146\n      auc_2v3: 0.5497\n      ci_1v2_lower: 0.6045\n      jsd_0v1: 0.2394\n      jsd_1v2: 0.0130\n      ordinal_accuracy: 0.3685\n    result_rationale: >\n      OLMo CI lower=0.6045 仅 +0.45pp above θ=0.60——在 worst-case 下审稿人将其标记为 \"borderline\n      pass, θ-dependent\"。如果 θ 从 0.60 上调至 0.61 或 0.62（审稿人认为合理的 sensitivity test），\n      OLMo 立即变为 K*=1。这使得 8/9 K*=2 claim 退化为 7/9 或更少。OLMo 是 1B 模型，被归类为\n      \"small model that doesn't generate very well\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Pairwise AUC, OLMo row highlighted as borderline\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"θ-sensitivity plot showing OLMo flips at θ≈0.605\"\n    analysis: >\n      OLMo 是 worst-case 下的 soft vulnerability：CI lower 几乎踩线，θ-sensitivity 下很容易翻转。\n      审稿人如果要求 θ=0.65 作为 \"meaningful effect size\"，OLMo 和 Qwen-cont 都会变 K*=1，\n      C4 从 8/9 K*=2 降至 6/9，narrative 从 \"dominant mode\" 退化为 \"slight majority\"。\n\n  - name: \"Qwen-7B C4 Cross-Scale\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-7B, C4 5K docs, depth 0-5, scorer=Qwen2.5-1.5B\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 2\n      auc_0v1: 0.9644\n      auc_1v2: 0.6178\n      auc_2v3: 0.5460\n      ci_1v2_lower: 0.6079\n      ci_2v3_upper: 0.5594\n    result_rationale: >\n      Qwen-7B C4 K*=2 成立（CI lower=0.6079, +0.79pp），但 margin 较小。Worst-case 下审稿人\n      注意到 0v1 AUC=0.9644 远低于小模型（Pythia 0.9932, OLMo 0.997），说明 7B 模型生成的 gen-1\n      文本已经更接近 human text——这意味着更大模型的 0v1 区分度在下降。审稿人可能推断 \"70B+ models\n      would have even lower 0v1 AUC, and 1v2 would drop below θ, making K*=1 the norm\n      at scale\"，直接挑战 scale generalization。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Scale comparison (1.5B vs 7B vs 14B) with 0v1 trend\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"0v1 AUC vs model scale plot showing declining trend\"\n    analysis: >\n      7B scale 确认 K*=2 但暴露了 scale-dependent 0v1 decline trend。Worst-case 下审稿人\n      据此论证 \"K*=2 is a small-model artifact; at frontier scale, even 0v1 detection\n      will become unreliable\"。14B (AUC 0v1=0.9598) 延续下降趋势，加剧此担忧。\n\n  - name: \"LLaMA-8B C4 Cross-Family\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-018\"\n    description: \"LLaMA-3.1-8B, continuation mode, C4 5K docs, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 2\n      auc_0v1: 0.9225\n      auc_1v2: 0.6123\n      auc_2v3: 0.5274\n      ci_1v2_lower: 0.6028\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLaMA-8B CI lower=0.6028 仅 +0.28pp above θ——worst-case 下这是 C4 实验中最脆弱的 K*=2\n      判定。0v1 AUC=0.9225 是所有 C4 模型中最低的，说明 LLaMA 生成的 gen-1 文本最接近 human。\n      审稿人直接指出 \"LLaMA-8B is already at the margin; LLaMA-70B would almost certainly\n      fall below θ\"。加上 cross-scorer 使用 Qwen-1.5B（不同家族、不同 tokenizer），信号衰减\n      是预期中的——但审稿人可能认为这是 scorer inadequacy 而非 genuine K*=2。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: LLaMA row with CI callout\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"CI forest plot with LLaMA near θ boundary\"\n    analysis: >\n      LLaMA-8B 是 worst-case 下 C4 K*=2 的最薄弱环节。CI lower=0.6028 意味着在 bootstrap\n      的 2.5th percentile 仅以 0.28pp 过关。任何关于 θ 选择的质疑都能翻转此结果。审稿人会指出\n      LLaMA 系列是当前最广泛使用的开源模型，如果其 K*=2 不稳健，实践价值大打折扣。\n\n  - name: \"Mistral-7B C4 Cross-Family\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-019\"\n    description: \"Mistral-7B-v0.3, continuation mode, C4 5K docs, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 1\n      auc_0v1: 0.9843\n      auc_1v2: 0.5935\n      auc_2v3: 0.5402\n      ci_1v2_lower: 0.5835\n      ci_1v2_upper: 0.6032\n      p_auc_leq_060: 0.9017\n    result_rationale: >\n      Mistral C4 K*=1 是已确认的 one-wash case。CI upper=0.6032 勉强触及 θ（P(AUC≤0.60)=90%），\n      cross-scorer 进一步降至 0.5695。Worst-case 下审稿人将 Mistral K*=1 与 LLaMA/OLMo/Qwen-cont\n      的 borderline K*=2 放在一起，论证 \"the real pattern is K*=1 for most modern models on\n      C4, with a few models barely crossing a conveniently chosen threshold\"。这直接攻击\n      8/9 K*=2 的 claim——如果 θ 上调 0.03pp，变为 5/9 K*=1。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Mistral C4 vs arXiv contrast row\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"AUC distribution plot highlighting Mistral as K*=1 outlier on C4\"\n    analysis: >\n      Mistral K*=1 on C4 but K*=3 on arXiv 是 domain dependence 的最强证据——这一点在\n      worst-case 下仍然成立且是唯一的 bright spot。但审稿人可能 reframe：Mistral 在 C4 上\n      K*=1 恰好说明 one-wash 是 more common than claimed，且与 Qwen-cont（CI lower=0.6015）\n      和 LLaMA（0.6028）合并看，C4 的 \"dominant K*=2\" 叙事站不住。\n\n  - name: \"Qwen-1.5B-Instruct Continuation Mode\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-017\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct continuation mode, C4 5K docs, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 2\n      auc_0v1: 0.9972\n      auc_1v2: 0.6114\n      auc_2v3: 0.5609\n      ci_1v2_lower: 0.6015\n      jsd_0v1: 0.2863\n      jsd_1v2: 0.0051\n    result_rationale: >\n      CI lower=0.6015 仅 +0.15pp above θ——这是 C4 所有 K*=2 判定中最边缘的。Worst-case 下\n      审稿人指出 cross-scorer validation (exp_A_alt_scorer) 中 Qwen-cont 被 Pythia 评分时\n      K*=1（AUC 1v2=0.5923），证明 K*=2 依赖于 same-family scorer。论文声称 scorer independence\n      但最边缘的 case 恰好在 cross-scorer 下 fail，这在审稿人看来是 \"selective reporting\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Qwen-cont same-scorer vs cross-scorer comparison\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"CI error bar plot with θ line, Qwen-cont nearly touching\"\n    analysis: >\n      Qwen-cont 是 worst-case 下的 Achilles heel。CI lower=0.6015 + cross-scorer K*=1\n      组合直接威胁 \"8/9 K*=2\" 的核心叙事。审稿人完全有理由要求 cross-scorer 作为 canonical\n      condition，此时 C4 K*=2 从 8/9 变为 ≤7/9（OLMo cross-scorer 未明确测试但预期也边缘），\n      且最边缘的几个 data points 全部依赖 θ=0.60。\n\n  - name: \"Qwen-1.5B Base Model C4\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-016\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-1.5B base continuation mode, C4 5K docs, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 2\n      auc_0v1: 0.987\n      auc_1v2: 0.6262\n      auc_2v3: 0.5496\n      ci_1v2_lower: 0.6168\n    result_rationale: >\n      Base model CI lower=0.6168（+1.7pp above θ）比 Instruct 更稳健。但 worst-case 下审稿人\n      注意到 base vs instruct 差异不显著（CI overlap），质疑 \"if base and instruct give the\n      same K*, what does this say about the generality of the finding?\" 结论是 K*=2\n      对 alignment 不敏感——这本身可以是正面发现，但在 worst-case framing 下被审稿人忽略。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Base vs Instruct comparison\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Base model 是 C4 上相对安全的 data point（margin +1.7pp）。Worst-case 下不是攻击重点，\n      但也不增加额外信息——审稿人认为 base/instruct 不影响 K* 是 \"expected, not interesting\"。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # C1' Domain Ablation — Wikipedia\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Wikipedia Domain Ablation (Qwen-1.5B)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-023\"\n    description: \"Wikipedia seed, Qwen2.5-1.5B base, continuation, 5K docs, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 2\n      auc_1v2: 0.6193\n      auc_2v3: 0.5498\n      note: \"same-family scorer; cross-scorer controls reduce to K*=1\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Qwen self-scorer 给 Wiki K*=2，但 D060 cross-family scorer（Pythia）证实 K*=1。\n      Worst-case 下审稿人将此视为 scorer confound 的 poster child：\"your own analysis shows\n      same-family scoring inflates K* by +1 on Wikipedia, yet you report K*=2 in the\n      same table as other models?\" 论文虽然在正文报 scorer-controlled K*=1，但审稿人质疑\n      为什么需要额外实验来发现这个问题——暗示其他域也可能有未检测到的 confound。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Wiki K* with scorer confound annotation\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scorer confound illustration: same-family vs cross-family\"\n    analysis: >\n      Wiki K*=1 在 scorer control 后是 robust 的（6 models all K*=1）。但 worst-case 下\n      scorer confound 的 existence 本身成为攻击向量：审稿人质疑 \"if you need cross-family\n      scoring to get correct K* on Wikipedia, how do you know C4 K*=2 isn't also inflated?\"\n      这迫使论文对每个 domain×model 组合都做 cross-scorer validation——资源约束下无法完成。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # C1' Domain Ablation — arXiv\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"arXiv Domain Ablation (Qwen-1.5B)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-024\"\n    description: \"arXiv abstracts, Qwen2.5-1.5B base, continuation, 5K docs, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 3\n      auc_0v1: 0.9946\n      auc_1v2: 0.858\n      auc_2v3: 0.6427\n      ci_2v3_lower: 0.6275\n      jsd_0v1: 0.171\n      jsd_1v2: 0.057\n      jsd_2v3: 0.020\n    result_rationale: >\n      arXiv K*=3 是 worst-case 下最稳健的发现：5/5 domain-competent models 一致，CI margin\n      充足（+2.75pp）。但审稿人会质疑：\"arXiv abstracts 是高度结构化的专业文本，current LLMs\n      生成的 arXiv 文本质量低（citation hallucination, formula errors），K*=3 可能仅反映\n      生成质量差而非 domain structural complexity。\" 另外 arXiv 在 web 污染场景中不是主要\n      concern——审稿人认为 \"who cares about arXiv K*=3 when the real problem is web text?\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: arXiv pairwise AUC across 5 models\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"arXiv vs C4 JSD cliff comparison\"\n    analysis: >\n      arXiv K*=3 在 worst-case 下从 \"domain hierarchy crown jewel\" 变为 \"niche finding\n      with limited practical relevance\"。审稿人承认它 cross-validated 但认为 practical\n      implications 弱（谁在 curate arXiv data?），且 K*=3 vs K*=2 的差异仅一步——\n      \"so structured text resists one more pass, is that really a paper?\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # C1' Decoding & Robustness\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Decoding Strategy Ablation (Qwen-1.5B)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-1.5B: greedy/nucleus p=0.9/T=0.7/T=1.2, C4 5K, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star_all_configs: 2\n      auc_1v2_range: [0.6862, 0.7037]\n      auc_1v2_greedy: 0.6892\n      auc_1v2_nuc09: 0.6862\n      auc_1v2_t07: 0.6885\n      auc_1v2_t12: 0.7037\n      note: \"nuc09 2v3 CI upper=0.601 crosses θ\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      4 种解码策略均 K*=2，但 nuc09 的 2v3 CI upper=0.601 几乎触及 θ，暗示 K*=3 在某些\n      decoding 下 borderline 可能。Worst-case 下审稿人承认 K* 对 decoding 不变，但指出\n      \"decoding invariance is expected — all strategies sample from the same distribution,\n      temperature merely scales logits. This is not a surprising finding.\" 实验成功但\n      不增加 novelty。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: 4 decoding × pairwise AUC matrix\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Decoding strategy comparison bar chart\"\n    analysis: >\n      Decoding invariance 在 worst-case 下被视为 \"sanity check, not contribution\"。\n      审稿人不会因此扣分但也不加分。唯一风险：nuc09 2v3 borderline 被拿来支撑 \"K* boundary\n      is fuzzy and θ-dependent\" 的论点。\n\n  - name: \"Pythia-1.4B Decoding Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-020\"\n    description: \"Pythia-1.4B: greedy/nuc09/T=0.7/T=1.2, C4 5K, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star_all_configs: 2\n      auc_1v2_greedy: 0.8838\n      auc_1v2_nuc09: 0.677\n      auc_1v2_t07: 0.7265\n      auc_1v2_t12: 0.6172\n    result_rationale: >\n      Pythia greedy 1v2=0.8838 异常高——因为 Pythia greedy 产生大量重复文本（repetition collapse），\n      创造了 artificial depth signal。Worst-case 下审稿人将此作为 \"your features capture\n      degeneracy, not depth\" 的证据。T=1.2（高温）AUC=0.6172 最低，接近 θ——审稿人指出\n      \"higher temperature narrows the depth signal gap, suggesting depth discrimination\n      is partly a temperature artifact\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Pythia decoding comparison with greedy anomaly flagged\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Pythia decoding 在 worst-case 下暴露了 feature sensitivity to text degeneracy。\n      Greedy 的 0.88 被攻击为 \"measuring repetition, not depth\"，T=1.2 的 0.62 被用来\n      论证 \"depth signal vanishes with sufficient randomness\"。K* 仍为 2 但可信度受损。\n\n  - name: \"Text Length Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-021\"\n    description: \"Qwen continuation, 128/256/512 tokens, C4 5K, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star_128: 2\n      k_star_256: 2\n      k_star_512: 2\n      auc_1v2_128: 0.6219\n      auc_1v2_256: 0.6282\n      auc_1v2_512: 0.6073\n      ci_512_1v2_lower: 0.5979\n      ci_512_1v2_verdict: BORDERLINE\n    result_rationale: >\n      512 token 条件 CI lower=0.5979 < θ=0.60——worst-case 下审稿人指出 \"at 512 tokens,\n      which is a realistic document length, K*=2 already fails bootstrap CI. Your\n      K*=2 finding is an artifact of short (128-256 token) text segments.\" 这直接威胁\n      ecological validity：真实文档通常远超 256 tokens，而 K*=2 在更长文本上不稳健。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Length × K* with 512-token CI flagged\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"AUC vs length curve showing 512-token drop\"\n    analysis: >\n      Length ablation 的 512-token borderline failure 是 worst-case 下的关键攻击点。\n      审稿人论证 \"if K*=2 only holds for short snippets, the practical applicability\n      to real-world document-level contamination detection is limited\"。这与 C3 的 negative\n      results 形成共振——方法论和实践价值同时被质疑。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # C1' Cross-Model Transfer & Scorer Independence\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cross-Model Transfer 4×4 Matrix\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-013\"\n    description: \"4 generators × 4 scorers transfer accuracy matrix\"\n    expected_results:\n      pythia_olmo_retention: \"91-92%\"\n      qwen_cont_others_retention: \"80-85%\"\n      qwen_rw_others_retention: \"61-63%\"\n      0v1_cross_all_above: 0.96\n      within_avg_pw_auc: 0.6099\n      cross_avg_pw_auc: 0.5905\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cross-model transfer 80-92% 是正面结果，但 worst-case 下审稿人注意到：\n      (1) Qwen-rewrite 跨模型仅 61-63%——generation mode 是比 model identity 更大的 confound；\n      (2) Cross average pw_auc=0.5905 < θ=0.60——跨模型平均辨别力不足以支撑 K*=2；\n      (3) 0v1 >0.96 说明 binary detection 已解决，fine-grained depth 不增加实践价值。\n      审稿人结论：\"binary contamination detection transfers perfectly; depth estimation\n      does not add practical value over binary.\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: 4×4 transfer matrix (accuracy and tau)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Transfer heatmap with within vs cross diagonal comparison\"\n    analysis: >\n      Transfer 实验在 worst-case 下产生 double-edged 结论：binary (0v1) 完美迁移→\n      既有 binary detectors 足够；fine-grained depth 迁移下降→depth estimation 不实用。\n      审稿人可能总结 \"the transferable signal is exactly what binary detectors already capture.\"\n\n  - name: \"4×4 Cross-Scorer Matrix\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-022\"\n    description: \"4 generators × 4 scorers, K* scorer independence\"\n    expected_results:\n      k2_count: 11\n      k1_count: 1\n      exception: \"qwen_cont256×pythia (1v2=0.5979, K*=1)\"\n      scorer_delta_max: 0.025\n    result_rationale: >\n      11/12 K*=2 看似稳健，但 worst-case 下审稿人关注：(1) 唯一 K*=1 case 恰好是\n      Qwen-cont（论文最边缘 case）被 Pythia score——证实 cross-scorer 下 Qwen-cont 不稳健；\n      (2) 此 matrix 基于 Pythia-greedy（1v2~0.88 repetition collapse）和 Qwen-base/cont，\n      不包含 Mistral/LLaMA 作为 generator，覆盖不完整；(3) cross_scorer_kstar_preservation_rate\n      下降至 0.65-0.75 range（worst-case 指标范围），如果扩展到所有 domain×model 组合。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Cross-scorer K* matrix\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-scorer 在 worst-case 下从 \"11/12 confirms K*=2\" 变为 \"the one failure\n      happens to be the most critical case (Qwen-cont), and the matrix doesn't include\n      the models most likely to fail (Mistral, LLaMA).\" 审稿人要求 full coverage 的\n      cross-scorer matrix（~30 combos for 4 domains × all models）——资源不可能满足。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # C1' Feature & Method Validation\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Feature Group Ablation & Degradation Ordering\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: \"Per feature group pairwise AUC and saturation depth analysis\"\n    expected_results:\n      cross_model_spearman_rho: \">0.85\"\n      shared_top_discriminators: \"surp_d1_std, surp_std, surp_d2_std\"\n      limitation_1v2_weakness: \"τ~0.37 at 1v2 pair\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Feature ordering 跨模型 ρ>0.85 是正面结果，但 worst-case 下审稿人指出 1v2 pair 的\n      cross-model consistency 最弱（τ~0.37）——而 1v2 恰好是决定 K*=2 vs K*=1 的 boundary pair。\n      \"The one depth pair that matters most for your K* determination has the weakest\n      cross-model feature agreement.\" 加之 features 是 \"standard text statistics\n      (surprisal, entropy, etc.)\"，审稿人质疑 \"15D feature engineering is not a methodological\n      contribution; these are well-known text quality metrics repurposed.\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Feature ranking comparison across models\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Degradation ordering heatmap\"\n    analysis: >\n      Feature ablation 在 worst-case 下被降级为 \"expected results with known metrics\"。\n      1v2 inconsistency 被放大为 methodology weakness。审稿人总结 \"feature engineering\n      adds nothing new; surprisal-based features have been used in MGT detection since 2023.\"\n\n  - name: \"Bootstrap CI & Permutation Tests\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: \"θ sensitivity at 0.55/0.60/0.65/0.70 with bootstrap CI and permutation\"\n    expected_results:\n      all_1v2_ci_lower_above_060: true\n      most_marginal: \"Qwen-cont CI lower=0.6015 (+0.15pp)\"\n      theta_060_k2_count: \"8/9\"\n      theta_065_k2_count: \"~5/9\"\n      theta_070_k2_count: \"~2/9\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      θ-sensitivity 在 worst-case 下是审稿人的主要攻击工具：θ=0.60 下 8/9 K*=2，但\n      θ=0.65 下降至约 5/9，θ=0.70 下仅约 2/9。审稿人指出 \"Cohen's h=0.20 (θ=0.60) is\n      conventionally 'small effect size' — your K*=2 claim literally rests on a 'small'\n      effect. At 'medium' effect (h=0.50, θ≈0.73), virtually all models show K*=1.\"\n      Qwen-cont 的 +0.15pp margin 被视为 cherry-picked threshold 的典型证据。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: K* at multiple θ values\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"K* vs θ sensitivity curve for all models\"\n    analysis: >\n      θ-sensitivity 是 worst-case 的核心弱点之一。审稿人可以合理要求 θ=0.65 作为\n      minimum \"practically meaningful\" threshold，此时 K*=2 的 dominant mode claim 崩塌。\n      论文的 permutation test 只证明 AUC ≠ 0.50（非随机），不证明 AUC 达到 \"meaningful\" 水平。\n      Cohen's h=0.20 defense 在 ML 社区不如在心理学中 convincing。\n\n  - name: \"Neural Probe (Learned Representations)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-015\"\n    description: \"Frozen embeddings + MLP vs 15D features across 3 models\"\n    expected_results:\n      pythia_k_neural: 2\n      olmo_k_neural: 2\n      qwen_k_neural: 3\n      key: \"Neural K* is model-dependent (Qwen=3 only under self-scorer)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Neural probe 本应证明 \"K*=2 is representation-intrinsic\"，但结果 model-dependent：\n      Qwen self-scorer K*_neural=3 > K*_15D=2，而 Pythia/OLMo K*_neural=2 = K*_15D。\n      Worst-case 下审稿人解读为 \"the neural probe shows that richer representations can\n      extract more depth signal (K*=3 for Qwen), meaning your 15D features are a\n      lossy bottleneck that artificially caps K* at 2. K*=2 is a feature engineering\n      artifact, not a data-intrinsic boundary.\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Neural probe vs 15D K* comparison\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Neural probe 的 model-dependent K* 在 worst-case 下直接反驳 \"K*=2 is data-intrinsic\"\n      的 claim。如果 Qwen neural probe 达到 K*=3，说明 information exists at depth 2v3\n      但 15D features 太粗糙无法捕获。审稿人总结：\"your K* is a property of your measurement\n      apparatus, not the data.\" 论文将此 reframe 为 \"model-free features give consistent K*\"\n      的 practical advantage，但审稿人不买账。\n\n  - name: \"Ordinal vs Multinomial vs Regression Baselines\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: \"CORAL ordinal vs multiclass LightGBM vs ordinal logistic regression\"\n    expected_results:\n      obd_lgbm_best_acc: 0.4229\n      multiclass_lgbm_acc: 0.4182\n      ordinal_logreg_acc: 0.3636\n      obd_vs_multiclass_delta: \"+0.47pp\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      OBD-LightGBM 仅比 multiclass LightGBM 好 0.47pp accuracy（42.3% vs 41.8%），\n      ordinal structure 的 advantage 微乎其微。Worst-case 下审稿人指出 \"ordinal modeling\n      adds complexity without meaningful improvement; a simple multiclass classifier\n      performs nearly identically, undermining the claim that depth has ordinal structure\n      worth exploiting.\" 此外所有方法 accuracy < 43%（6-class，random=16.7%），绝对\n      performance 不 impressive。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: 3 methods × 3 models comparison\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Ordinal baseline 在 worst-case 下证明 ordinal structure 几乎无 practical benefit。\n      审稿人将此与 C3 negative results 联系：\"even your ordinal classifier barely beats\n      multiclass, and your K*-aware filtering barely beats binary — the ordinal/depth\n      information has no actionable value.\"\n\n  - name: \"LLM Zero-Shot Depth Estimation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: \"GPT-5.5 / Claude Opus 4.6 zero-shot depth estimation, 500 samples\"\n    expected_results:\n      gpt55_5class_acc: 0.332\n      claude_5class_acc: 0.331\n      odb_baseline_acc: 0.386\n      binary_acc_both: \"~88%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Frontier LLMs 5-class accuracy ~33% < OBD 38.6%——看似证明需要专门方法。但 worst-case\n      下审稿人指出：(1) 33% vs 38.6% 差距不大（McNemar p>0.05 不显著），不能 claim OBD\n      \"significantly outperforms\"；(2) binary 88% 说明 depth-0 detection 已被 LLM 解决，\n      而 fine-grained depth 对所有方法（包括 OBD）都失败——\"your method is slightly better\n      at a task nobody can do well\"；(3) 500 samples 太少（power concerns）。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: LLM vs OBD accuracy comparison\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-depth accuracy breakdown showing all methods fail at depth 1-4\"\n    analysis: >\n      LLM baseline 在 worst-case 下被 turned against the paper：\"all methods fail at\n      fine-grained depth estimation, including yours. The task as defined may be\n      fundamentally too hard to be useful.\" Binary detection at 88% 强化 \"just do binary\"\n      的审稿人立场。\n\n  - name: \"Binary Detector Confidence as Depth Proxy\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-012\"\n    description: \"DivEye/Binoculars score Spearman correlation with true depth\"\n    expected_results:\n      binary_kstar: 1\n      obd_kstar: 2\n      max_spearman_rho: 0.46\n      six_class_acc_max: 0.199\n    result_rationale: >\n      Binary detectors K*=1 vs OBD K*=2 的差异证明深度信息超越 binary。但 worst-case 下\n      审稿人质疑：\"OBD uses 15 hand-crafted features and a trained classifier, while\n      DivEye/Binoculars are single-score methods designed for binary detection — the\n      comparison is unfair. A fair comparison would train a classifier on DivEye features\n      across depth levels.\" 6-class accuracy ≤19.9% 再次证明 fine-grained depth 对所有方法\n      都不 work。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Binary vs OBD comparison\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Non-monotonic AUC plot for binary detectors\"\n    analysis: >\n      Binary detector comparison 在 worst-case 下被视为 \"strawman baseline\"——用单分数\n      binary 工具对比 15D trained classifier 不公平。审稿人可能要求与 \"binary detector\n      features + depth-aware classifier\" 对比。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # C1' Retrain Chain & Ecological Validity\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Retrain Chain (Pythia-1.4B)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: \"Pythia-1.4B LoRA retrain chain, C4 5K, depth 0-4\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: \">=4\"\n      auc_0v1: 0.9847\n      auc_1v2: 0.9484\n      auc_2v3: 0.8888\n      auc_3v4: 0.7982\n    result_rationale: >\n      Retrain K*≥4 大幅超越 prompt-chain K*=2——但 worst-case 下审稿人认为 \"retrain-chain\n      detects LoRA adaptation artifacts, not text-intrinsic depth signal. K*≥4 is an\n      artifact of your experimental setup, not a property of recursive contamination.\"\n      更重要的是，retrain chain 与 prompt chain 的 K* 差距（2 vs ≥4）反而证明 K* depends\n      heavily on the contamination mechanism，而论文只测了一种 mechanism (prompt-chain)——\n      ecological validity concern 加剧。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Prompt-chain vs retrain-chain AUC comparison\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"K* divergence between contamination mechanisms\"\n    analysis: >\n      Retrain chain 在 worst-case 下从 \"ecological validity evidence\" 变为 \"evidence\n      of mechanism-dependence\"。审稿人论证 K*=2 只是 prompt-chain specific，真实世界\n      可能有 K*=7（retrain）或 K*=1（其他机制），论文的 K*=2 claim 无法泛化。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # C1' Additional Robustness\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Subsampling Power Curve\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-028\"\n    description: \"C4 subsampling n={1000,...,5000} × 10 resamples\"\n    expected_results:\n      min_n_100pct: 2000\n      n1000_rate: 0.3\n      n2000_rate: 1.0\n      n5000_auc: 0.6288\n    result_rationale: >\n      n≥2000 给 100% detection——但 worst-case 下审稿人指出 \"the fact that you need n=2000\n      samples to reliably detect K*=2 means the effect size is tiny. For comparison,\n      binary detection (0v1) works with n=100. This confirms K*=2 is a statistical\n      artifact visible only in aggregate, not a practically useful signal for individual\n      documents.\" n=1000 仅 30% detection rate 强化 \"weak signal\" 叙事。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Power curve with detection rates\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Power curve plot\"\n    analysis: >\n      Power curve 在 worst-case 下被 used against the paper：大样本需求 = 小效应量 = \n      不实用。审稿人对比 binary detection 的 near-perfect per-sample accuracy 与 depth\n      estimation 的 n=2000 aggregate requirement。\n\n  - name: \"LaTeX Markup Removal Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-027\"\n    description: \"arXiv text with LaTeX stripped, verify K*=3 preserved\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star_preserved: true\n      auc_2v3_original: 0.6436\n      auc_2v3_stripped: 0.6229\n      delta_2v3: -0.021\n    result_rationale: >\n      K*=3 after LaTeX removal is positive——但 worst-case 下 2v3 AUC 从 0.6436 降至 0.6229\n      （-2.1pp），margin 从 +4.3pp 收窄至 +2.3pp above θ。审稿人指出 \"LaTeX removal costs\n      you nearly half your safety margin. What about other formatting artifacts (citation\n      brackets, equation numbering, section headers)? Full markup removal might push\n      2v3 below θ.\" 实验被视为 incomplete ablation。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Original vs stripped AUC\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      LaTeX ablation 在 worst-case 下 partially succeeds 但暴露 format-dependency：\n      LaTeX 贡献了 ~2pp 的 signal，更彻底的 stripping 可能消除剩余 margin。审稿人要求\n      full-structure removal ablation（headers, citations, formulas 全部 normalize），\n      这个实验未做。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # C3 Filtering Experiments\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Downstream Filtering Evaluation (Qwen, C4)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: \"6 strategies × 5 seeds, continued pretraining, MMLU+HellaSwag\"\n    expected_results:\n      binary_ours_mmlu: \"0.5941±0.0008\"\n      no_filter_mmlu: \"0.5865±0.0010\"\n      delta_mmlu: \"+0.0076\"\n      delta_hellaswag: \"+0.0063\"\n      best_strategy: \"binary-ours\"\n      graduated_a09_mmlu: \"0.5892±0.0008\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Binary outperforms all——但 worst-case 下审稿人质疑：(1) 所有策略都 degrade vs\n      base model（0.6018 MMLU），\"your best filtering still makes the model worse than\n      doing nothing\"；(2) binary vs no_filter delta=0.76pp MMLU——统计显著但 practically\n      meaningless；(3) graduated α monotone increasing 说明 \"more filtering is always\n      better regardless of depth awareness\"——K* information 没有 incremental value over\n      simple quality threshold；(4) DSIR 差于 no_filter，说明 distribution matching 反而有害，\n      但这是 DSIR 的问题不是本文的贡献。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: All 6 strategies × MMLU/HellaSwag\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Strategy ranking bar chart\"\n    analysis: >\n      C3 在 worst-case 下的叙事崩塌：binary beats graduated（不符合 \"depth-aware curation\n      is better\" 的 hypothesis），所有策略 < base model，delta < 1pp。审稿人总结 \"K*\n      provides no curation benefit beyond what a simple binary classifier already gives.\"\n      c3_binary_vs_nofilter_hellaswag_delta_pp 在 3.8-6.1pp range（dose response 中），\n      但单个 30% ratio 下仅 ~6pp——不足以 justify depth estimation pipeline 的复杂性。\n\n  - name: \"Contamination Dose-Response\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: \"10%/30%/50% contamination ratio × 3 strategies × 5 seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      binary_advantage_hellaswag_10pct: \"+0.38pp\"\n      binary_advantage_hellaswag_30pct: \"+0.61pp\"\n      binary_advantage_hellaswag_50pct: \"+0.51pp\"\n      graduated_vs_nofilter: \"identical at all ratios\"\n      all_p_values_hellaswag: \"≤0.004\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Binary filtering 在所有 ratio 下显著优于 no_filter（HellaSwag），但 graduated = no_filter\n      在所有 ratio 下完全一致。Worst-case 下这是 C3 的 death blow：dose-response 本应展示\n      \"as contamination increases, depth-aware filtering becomes more important\"，实际结果是\n      \"graduated filtering provides zero benefit at any contamination level\"。审稿人结论：\n      \"binary filtering works because it removes synthetic text; the depth dimension K* adds\n      nothing. Your headline claim C3 is falsified by your own dose-response analysis.\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: 3 ratios × 3 strategies with p-values\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dose-response curve with graduated=no_filter overlap\"\n    analysis: >\n      Dose-response 在 worst-case 下完全否定 C3 的 depth-aware curation hypothesis。\n      Binary 的优势仅来自 \"remove synthetic text\" 而非 \"use depth information\"。\n      审稿人会质疑论文的 claim rewrite——如果 C3 只是 \"binary filtering works\"，这已被\n      Drayson et al. (2025) 证明，不是新贡献。\n\n  - name: \"Pythia-1.4B Filtering Replication\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-025\"\n    description: \"Pythia LoRA rank=8, 3 strategies × 3 seeds, MMLU+HellaSwag\"\n    expected_results:\n      binary_ours_mmlu: \"0.2585±0.0004\"\n      no_filter_mmlu: \"0.2568±0.0012\"\n      delta_max: \"0.0017 (noise)\"\n      conclusion: \"negative — all strategies identical\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Pythia filtering 完全 negative：三种策略 within noise（max delta 0.17pp MMLU）。\n      Worst-case 下审稿人直接 quote：\"your filtering experiment fails to replicate on a\n      second model, suggesting the Qwen result (exp-006) is model-specific.\" C3 的 scope\n      从 \"general principle\" 退化为 \"works on Qwen-1.5B with C4 data only\"——太窄无法\n      作为 conference contribution。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Pythia filtering negative result\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Pythia negative result 在 worst-case 下彻底瓦解 C3 的 generalizability。Qwen exp-006\n      可能是 model-specific artifact（Qwen-1.5B 的特定 tokenizer/architecture 恰好对\n      binary filtering 敏感）。审稿人不会接受 \"C3 validated for one model configuration\"\n      作为 conference contribution。\n\n  - name: \"arXiv Graduated vs Binary Filtering\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-026\"\n    description: \"arXiv depth chain (K*=3), 3 strategies × 5 seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      graduated_mmlu: \"0.5900±0.0011\"\n      binary_mmlu: \"0.5876±0.0004\"\n      no_filter_mmlu: \"0.5899±0.0008\"\n      conclusion: \"negative — all identical\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      arXiv K*=3 是 C3 的关键测试场——如果 K*=3 则 graduated 应优于 binary（depth 3 信息\n      有增量价值）。结果完全 negative。Worst-case 下这是最致命的 C3 failure：唯一一个\n      K*>2 的域上，depth-aware filtering 仍然无效。审稿人总结 \"K* characterization (C1')\n      and practical curation (C3) are disconnected — knowing K* doesn't help you curate\n      data better.\" 这直接攻击论文的 motivation：\"why measure K* if it has no downstream\n      utility?\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: arXiv 3 strategies × MMLU/HellaSwag\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      arXiv filtering negative 是 worst-case 下的致命证据。Paper 的 story spine 声称\n      \"domain-dependent K* provides actionable curation guidance\"，但 K*=3 域上的 curation\n      完全无效。审稿人在 C3 上的 verdict 将是 \"insufficient practical contribution\"——\n      与 worst-case 核心假设完全一致。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # C2 Methodology & Baselines\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Naturalistic Validation (Common Crawl)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-014\"\n    description: \"Common Crawl 2025/2026 snapshot depth prediction + correlation\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"planned/not_executed\"\n      predicted_spearman_with_alignscore: [0.15, 0.30]\n      predicted_spearman_with_vocab_richness: [0.20, 0.35]\n      predicted_depth_distribution_mode: 0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst-case 下此实验未执行或结果令人失望：(1) Common Crawl 样本的 predicted depth\n      分布高度偏向 depth 0（大部分 web 文本仍为 human-written），缺少 depth>1 的 ground\n      truth 验证；(2) 与 AlignScore 的 correlation 微弱（ρ~0.15-0.30）——depth 预测\n      与独立质量指标不一致；(3) 无法验证 K* boundary 在 wild data 上是否成立（无 ground\n      truth depth labels）。审稿人标注为 \"critical missing experiment for ecological validity\"。\n      如果已执行，低 correlation 被解读为 \"your lab-measured K* doesn't transfer to real-world\n      contamination patterns.\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Predicted depth distribution (if executed)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Depth prediction histogram of CC samples\"\n    analysis: >\n      Naturalistic validation 缺失或失败在 worst-case 下是审稿人的主要 concern：\"all\n      your experiments are in controlled lab settings with clean prompt-chains. You\n      have zero evidence this works on real-world contaminated data.\" 即使执行了，低\n      correlation + 缺少 ground truth 也无法消除质疑。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Code Domain — RUNNING experiments (worst-case predictions)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Code Domain — Mistral-7B (RUNNING, worst-case prediction)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_code_mistral7b\"\n    description: \"Mistral-7B Code/Python depth chain, predicted K*=1\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 1\n      auc_0v1: [0.91, 0.95]\n      auc_1v2: [0.52, 0.58]\n      auc_2v3: [0.50, 0.53]\n      ci_1v2_upper: [0.55, 0.60]\n      jsd_1v2: [0.003, 0.006]\n    result_rationale: >\n      Mistral C4 已是 K*=1（AUC 1v2=0.5935），Code domain 对 Mistral 更不利：Mistral 的\n      code generation 能力虽优于 Pythia 但仍低于 Qwen/LLaMA code-tuned 变体。Code domain\n      的 syntactic regularity（indentation, brackets, keywords）使 Mistral 的 code 生成\n      快速 converge 到 template-like patterns，1v2 信号在一次迭代后即消失。AUC 1v2 预期\n      0.52-0.58，低于 C4 的 0.5935——Code 的强结构约束加速了信息丧失。Cross-family scorer\n      (Qwen) 可能进一步降低 AUC（如 C4 上 Mistral cross-scorer 从 0.5935 降至 0.5695）。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Code domain cross-model K* summary with Mistral=1\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Mistral Code K*=1 在 worst-case 下意味着 Code ceiling=2 的证据从 2/3 变为 2/4。\n      加上 Pythia Code K*=1（已确认），Code domain 中 K*=1 的模型（Mistral + Pythia）\n      与 K*=2 的模型（Qwen-1.5B + LLaMA-8B）形成 2:2 split——无法建立 ceiling=2。\n\n  - name: \"Code Domain — Qwen-7B (RUNNING, worst-case prediction)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_code_qwen7b\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-7B Code/Python depth chain, predicted K*=1 or borderline\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 1\n      auc_0v1: [0.93, 0.96]\n      auc_1v2: [0.54, 0.60]\n      auc_2v3: [0.50, 0.54]\n      ci_1v2_upper: [0.58, 0.62]\n      note: \"CI may cross θ but point estimate below\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Qwen-7B 在 C4 上 1v2=0.6178（K*=2），但 Code domain 的 generation mode 不同：code\n      completion 比 web text continuation 更 constrained（syntax, indentation）。Qwen-7B\n      虽然有 code training data，但 code domain 的 structural regularity 加速 depth signal\n      消失。预期 AUC 1v2=0.54-0.60——point estimate 可能 < θ 或 borderline。如果 CI upper\n      恰好过 0.60 但 point estimate < 0.60，审稿人将判定 K*=1。Worst-case 下 Qwen-7B\n      Code 的 code competence 不足以在第二代文本中保留 distinguishable structure。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Qwen-7B C4 vs Code comparison\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Qwen-7B Code K*=1 使 Code domain 成为 2/5 K*=2（仅 Qwen-1.5B 和 LLaMA-8B），\n      直接触发 worst-case 的核心假设。Domain ceiling=2 退化为 \"two specific models happen\n      to achieve K*=2 on Code\"——不是 domain property 而是 model property。审稿人将\n      Code 和 C4 合并分析：C4 有 Mistral K*=1 exception，Code 有 Mistral+Qwen-7B+Pythia\n      K*=1——中间复杂度域的 K* 是 model-dependent 而非 domain-determined。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Additional RUNNING experiments\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Qwen-32B C4 (RUNNING, worst-case prediction)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_32b_c4\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-32B, C4 depth chain, worst-case prediction\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: [1, 2]\n      auc_0v1: [0.90, 0.94]\n      auc_1v2: [0.58, 0.62]\n      ci_1v2_lower: [0.57, 0.61]\n      note: \"borderline; may flip to K*=1\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      0v1 AUC declining trend with scale: 1.5B→0.997, 7B→0.9644, 14B→0.9598。\n      32B 预期 0v1 进一步下降至 0.90-0.94。1v2 AUC 趋势不明确（7B=0.6178, 14B=0.621,\n      scale 不单调），但 32B 生成的文本质量更高→depth signal 更弱。Worst-case 下 K*=1\n      或 borderline K*=2，进一步强化 \"K*=2 is a small-model phenomenon\" 的审稿人攻击线。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Scale trend 1.5B→7B→14B→32B\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"AUC vs scale trend plot with 32B prediction band\"\n    analysis: >\n      32B 结果如果 K*=1 或 borderline，审稿人将直接 extrapolate：\"at 70B+, K*=1 is\n      virtually certain. Your K*=2 finding is limited to ≤14B models and has no relevance\n      to the frontier models that dominate real-world text generation.\" 这是 scale\n      generalization concern 的 worst-case 实现。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Retrain Chain Extended (from registry, supporting C1')\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Qwen Retrain Chain Depth 7\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_qwen_retrain_depth7\"\n    description: \"Qwen-1.5B retrain chain extended to depth 7\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 7\n      auc_6v7: 0.641\n      ci_6v7_lower: 0.6376\n    result_rationale: >\n      Retrain K*=7 跨两个模型家族一致（Qwen 6v7=0.641, Pythia 6v7=0.634）——但 worst-case\n      下审稿人认为这完全是 LoRA artifact：\"7 rounds of LoRA fine-tuning accumulate vocabulary\n      narrowing and repetition bias that are trivially detectable. This has nothing to do\n      with text-intrinsic information loss.\" Retrain K*=7 vs prompt K*=2 的 3.5x 差距\n      进一步证明 K* is mechanism-dependent, not data-intrinsic。审稿人可能要求 full\n      fine-tuning（非 LoRA）来排除 adapter-specific artifacts——这在计算资源上不可行。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Retrain-chain pairwise AUC depth 0-7\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Prompt-chain vs retrain-chain K* divergence plot\"\n    analysis: >\n      Retrain depth 7 在 worst-case 下被完全 dismissed 为 \"LoRA artifact study\"。\n      论文将其定位为 \"upper bound\"，但审稿人质疑 \"an upper bound from a different mechanism\n      tells you nothing about the mechanism you claim to study (prompt-chain).\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Wikipedia Multi-Model (from registry, supporting C1')\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Wikipedia Scorer Confound Control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_wiki_scorer_confound + exp_wiki_scorer_confound_1b5\"\n    description: \"Cross-family scorer validation on Wikipedia\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star_after_control: 1\n      auc_1v2_cross_scorer: 0.587\n      delta_from_same_scorer: -0.024\n    result_rationale: >\n      Wiki scorer confound confirmed：same-family scorer inflates K* by +1（K*=2→1）。\n      Worst-case 下审稿人将此作为 systematic concern：\"if Wikipedia has a +1 scorer bias,\n      how do you know C4 doesn't have a similar bias? You only tested cross-scorer\n      on a subset of conditions.\" 论文承认 scorer confound 是 domain-specific，但审稿人\n      不接受 \"absence of evidence is not evidence of absence\"——C4 可能有未检测到的 bias。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Wiki same-scorer vs cross-scorer K*\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Wiki scorer confound 在 worst-case 下从 \"transparent disclosure\" 变为 \"systematic\n      methodology flaw\"。审稿人要求所有 domain×model 组合都做 cross-scorer validation\n      （total ~40 combos），论文仅完成 ~15，覆盖不足。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # arXiv Cross-Scorer (from registry, supporting C1')\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"arXiv Cross-Scorer Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_arXiv_qwen7b_crossscorer + others\"\n    description: \"arXiv cross-family scorer validation\"\n    expected_results:\n      qwen7b_crossscorer_k_star: 2\n      qwen7b_crossscorer_2v3: 0.5989\n      qwen1b5_crossscorer_k_star: 3\n      llama8b_crossscorer_k_star: 3\n      mistral7b_crossscorer_k_star: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      arXiv cross-scorer 揭示 Qwen-7B K*=3→2 drop（2v3=0.5989, just below θ）。\n      Worst-case 下审稿人指出 \"even arXiv K*=3 is not fully scorer-robust: one model\n      drops to K*=2 under cross-scoring. Cross-scorer preservation rate is 3/4=75%,\n      not 100%.\" 这落在 worst-case 指标范围 cross_scorer_kstar_preservation_rate=0.65-0.75\n      内。审稿人论证 arXiv 的 \"robust K*=3\" 也有 scorer confound 的 shadow。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: arXiv self-scorer vs cross-scorer comparison\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      arXiv cross-scorer 在 worst-case 下暴露 75% preservation rate（Qwen-7B drops），\n      比 C4 的 11/12=92% 低。如果 Code domain 也做 cross-scorer，preservation rate 预期\n      更低（worst-case 0.65-0.75）。审稿人总结：\"scorer independence is domain-dependent\n      and never fully holds, meaning K* is not purely text-intrinsic as claimed.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Code Domain Completed (from registry)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Code Domain — Qwen-1.5B\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_code_qwen1b5\"\n    description: \"Qwen-1.5B Code/Python depth chain\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 2\n      auc_0v1: 0.9388\n      auc_1v2: 0.7382\n      auc_2v3: 0.530\n      jsd_1v2: 0.0443\n      jsd_2v3: 0.0038\n    result_rationale: >\n      Qwen-1.5B Code K*=2 with strong margin（1v2=0.7382, +13.8pp above θ），JSD cliff\n      11.7x at 1v2→2v3。但 worst-case 下此 strong result 被 contextualized：(1) Qwen-1.5B\n      是 Qwen 家族的最小模型，其 code 能力有限→high 1v2 可能反映 \"poor code generation\n      easily detected\" 而非 domain property；(2) 仅 2/5 Code models 达到 K*=2，不足以\n      claim ceiling=2；(3) cross-scorer (Pythia) 确认 K*=2（0.7197）但 margin 下降 1.85pp。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Code domain model summary\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"JSD cliff comparison: Code vs C4 pattern difference\"\n    analysis: >\n      Qwen-1.5B Code K*=2 是 Code domain 最强的 data point，但 worst-case 下审稿人\n      将其与 Pythia K*=1 合并看：小模型在 Code 上 K*=1（Pythia）或 K*=2（Qwen），\n      取决于 code competence。如果 7B models 也 K*=1，则 Code ceiling=2 的证据 collapses。\n\n  - name: \"Code Domain — LLaMA-8B\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_code_llama8b\"\n    description: \"LLaMA-3.1-8B Code/Python depth chain\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 2\n      auc_0v1: 0.9161\n      auc_1v2: 0.7394\n      auc_2v3: 0.5112\n      jsd_1v2: 0.047\n      jsd_2v3: 0.0035\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLaMA Code K*=2 cross-family confirmed（1v2=0.7394, scored by Qwen）。但 worst-case\n      下审稿人注意到 2v3=0.5112 非常低（几乎 random），JSD cliff 13.5x。Code 的 K*=2\n      是 \"sharp cliff\"（1v2 很高但 2v3 几乎 chance），与 C4 的 gradual decline 不同。\n      审稿人可能认为 \"Code K*=2 simply means gen-1 code is detectable (trivially), but\n      by gen-2 it's already converged to generic code patterns.\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: LLaMA Code vs C4 comparison\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      LLaMA Code K*=2 提供 cross-family evidence，但 worst-case 下 sharp cliff pattern\n      被解读为 \"trivial gen-1 detection + immediate collapse\"——与 C4 的 more nuanced\n      depth signal 不同。审稿人可能质疑 Code 和 C4 是否真的 share ceiling=2 当 signal\n      dynamics 完全不同。\n\n  - name: \"Code Domain — Pythia-1.4B\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_code_pythia1b4\"\n    description: \"Pythia-1.4B Code/Python depth chain\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 1\n      auc_0v1: 0.9592\n      auc_1v2: 0.5983\n      auc_2v3: 0.5215\n      note: \"fold-level 1v2 varies: 3/5 folds > 0.60 but aggregate mean < θ\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Pythia Code K*=1 reflects code generation competence 不足（The Pile 训练，code\n      占比低）。Worst-case 下审稿人直接引用：\"3 of 5 folds give 1v2 > 0.60 but the mean\n      is 0.5983 — your K* determination is literally a coin flip at the fold level.\n      θ=0.60 applied to means (not per-fold) is another methodological choice that\n      favors your narrative.\" 这加剧 θ cherry-picking 的指控。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Pythia Code per-fold breakdown\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Pythia Code K*=1 在 worst-case 下与 Mistral Code K*=1（predicted）合并，形成\n      \"3/5 Code models at K*=1\" 的局面，使 Code ceiling=2 claim 不可持续。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Paired Statistics (from registry, supporting C3)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Paired Statistical Tests for Filtering\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_E_paired_stats\"\n    description: \"Holm-Bonferroni corrected paired tests for C3\"\n    expected_results:\n      mmlu_significant_pairs: \"8/15\"\n      hellaswag_significant_pairs: \"9/15\"\n      binary_vs_all_mmlu: \"all significant\"\n      graduated_a09_vs_dsir_corrected_p: 0.0523\n    result_rationale: >\n      MMLU 仅 8/15 pairs significant after Holm-Bonferroni correction（bugfix 后从 10/15\n      降至 8/15）。Worst-case 下审稿人注意到 (1) graduated_a09 vs DSIR corrected p=0.0523\n      不显著——graduated filtering 甚至不能 beat DSIR；(2) binary wins but graduated ≈ DSIR\n      ≈ no_filter——depth-aware 的 graduated 方法完全没有优势；(3) Cohen's d 值很高（>8）\n      是因为 within-seed variance 极低，不代表 practically large effects。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Holm-Bonferroni corrected p-value matrix\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Statistical tests 在 worst-case 下支持 binary-ours significance 但彻底否定\n      graduated filtering。\"Binary outperforms\" 是 uninteresting（Drayson et al. already showed\n      this），\"graduated fails\" 是 C3 的 core negative result。高 Cohen's d + tiny absolute\n      delta = \"statistically significant, practically irrelevant\"。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Additional Plan Experiments\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"OBD vs Multiclass Comparison (n=500)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_D_obd_n500\"\n    description: \"OBD accuracy vs LLM baselines with McNemar tests\"\n    expected_results:\n      obd_accuracy: 0.38\n      mcnemar_vs_gpt_p: 0.0809\n      mcnemar_vs_claude_p: 0.0693\n      mcnemar_significant: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      McNemar tests 不显著——OBD 与 frontier LLMs 在 5-class 上无显著差异。Worst-case 下\n      审稿人直接引用：\"your specialized 15-feature classifier does not significantly\n      outperform GPT-5.5 zero-shot on the task it was designed for.\" 这从 \"baseline\n      comparison\" 变为 \"our method is no better than prompting a frontier model.\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: OBD vs LLM McNemar results\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Non-significant McNemar 在 worst-case 下消除了 exp-011 的 positive framing。\n      审稿人看到 OBD=38% vs LLM=33%（p>0.05）会认为 \"no meaningful advantage from\n      specialized methodology — just use GPT.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Overall Worst-Case Summary\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Aggregate Worst-Case Assessment\"\n    plan_id: \"overall\"\n    description: \"Cross-experiment synthesis under worst-case scenario\"\n    expected_results:\n      domain_hierarchy_clean_fit: \"78-85%\"\n      code_ceiling2_support: \"2/5 models\"\n      c4_k2_at_theta060: \"8/9\"\n      c4_k2_at_theta065: \"~5/9\"\n      cross_scorer_preservation: \"65-75%\"\n      c3_validated_scope: \"Qwen-1.5B C4 binary only\"\n      c3_depth_aware_advantage: \"zero (graduated=no_filter everywhere)\"\n      estimated_reviewer_excitement: [2.8, 3.2]\n      emnlp_main_accept_prob: [0.05, 0.25]\n      emnlp_findings_prob: [0.30, 0.50]\n      aaai_with_70b_data_prob: [0.25, 0.40]\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst-case 的核心问题是 \"three-front attack\"：(1) K*≤3 trivial（审稿人不认为 bounded ≤3\n      是 surprising——\"of course models converge quickly, we knew that from model collapse\n      literature\"）；(2) C3 全面失败（graduated=no_filter, Pythia negative, arXiv negative）\n      → depth estimation 无 practical value；(3) θ=0.60 cherry-picking + scorer confound +\n      borderline CIs → K*=2 claim 的 statistical robustness 被质疑。三条线交汇时，审稿人\n      的 narrative 是 \"this paper measures something (K*) that is neither surprising (≤3)\n      nor useful (C3 fails) nor robust (θ-dependent), and the measurement methodology\n      (15D features) is standard text statistics.\" Reviewer excitement 2.8-3.2 对应\n      EMNLP \"Borderline Findings to Findings\" range——Main 几乎不可能（需要 4.0），Findings\n      需要 reframe 成功。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Summary K* across all domains × models\"\n      - \"Table: C3 filtering results synthesis\"\n      - \"Table: θ-sensitivity summary\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grand summary: domain × model K* heatmap with worst-case Code columns\"\n      - \"Reviewer concern mapping to experimental evidence\"\n    analysis: >\n      Reframe 策略在 worst-case 下的可行性评估：\n      (A) Information-theoretic rapid convergence：最可行。放弃 \"domain ceiling\" 作为\n      predictive framework，转为 descriptive finding \"K*≤3 across all tested conditions\"。\n      DPI 理论保证有限但不给上界→实证 ≤3 是 non-trivial bound。但审稿人仍可能认为\n      model collapse 文献已 implicitly 知道这一点。需要 very strong writing 来 differentiate\n      \"first systematic measurement with operational definition\" vs \"known phenomenon,\n      just quantified.\"\n      (B) Measurement methodology：次可行。15D features 是 standard text statistics，\n      审稿人不认为方法论本身是贡献。除非 reframe 为 \"first reproducible protocol for\n      depth estimation\" with open-source toolkit——methodology paper 在 EMNLP Findings\n      有先例但 excitement 低。\n      最终评估：worst-case 下 EMNLP Main 接收概率 5-25%（需要至少一位 champion reviewer），\n      Findings 30-50%（如果 reframe 成功）。AAAI 2027 backup 有更多时间补充 70B+ 数据\n      和改进 C3（larger-scale filtering with full fine-tuning），但 AAAI 对 NLP-specific\n      methodology 的 appetite 较低。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11303,"cache_read_input_tokens":67451,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11303},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"03f7a7fe-5346-4dc3-ab9a-d132249e2154","uuid":"af0e3ffb-fbf4-4743-90e4-eb10c7390460"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":492720,"duration_api_ms":494572,"num_turns":5,"result":"Now I have the full picture. Let me construct the worst-case scenario predictions for all 29 experiments in the plan, plus key running experiments that define this scenario.\n\n```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Code 域两个 pending 均 K*=1，domain ceiling=2 仅剩 Qwen-1.5B + LLaMA-8B 两个 data points（2/5），\n  无法独立于 C4 建立 Code ceiling=2。Domain hierarchy 从 4 级清晰阶梯退化为 Wiki=1（稳健）、arXiv=3（稳健）、\n  C4/Code 混杂（K*∈{1,2} model-dependent）。审稿人在 K* 范围 trivial、C3 failures、θ 任意性上多线质疑，\n  原始 \"domain ceiling framework\" framing 不可持续。需要 reframe：\n  (A) Information-theoretic rapid convergence — DPI 理论预测 K* 有限 + 实证首次证明 K*≤3 本身是核心发现，\n  不依赖 clean domain hierarchy；或\n  (B) Measurement methodology contribution — 首次提出可操作的 K* 测量方法论，domain hierarchy 降级为 first application。\n  仍冲 EMNLP（Findings 为现实预期），或用 AAAI deadline 补充 70B+ 模型实验。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # C1' Core K* Characterization — C4 Web Text\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"MVP Pilot Saturation (Qwen-1.5B rewrite)\"\n    plan_id: \"mvp-001\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct rewrite mode, C4 5K docs, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 2\n      auc_0v1: 0.9956\n      auc_1v2: 0.6957\n      auc_2v3: 0.5893\n      ci_1v2_lower: 0.6859\n      ci_2v3_upper: 0.5991\n      jsd_0v1: 0.2669\n      jsd_1v2: 0.0163\n    result_rationale: >\n      Rewrite mode AUC 1v2=0.6957 是所有 continuation 条件的 1.14x，但 worst-case 下审稿人将其\n      归因于 instruction-following style artifacts 而非 genuine depth signal。Cross-model transfer\n      仅 61-63% retention（vs continuation 80-92%）证实 rewrite 信号不泛化。这个结果在 worst-case\n      framing 下从 \"strongest K*=2 evidence\" 降级为 \"mode-specific pilot with limited generalizability\"，\n      削弱其作为核心证据的权重。审稿人可能直接质疑为什么 headline 实验用了最不可靠的 mode。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Pairwise AUC × depth pair, 标注 rewrite mode caveat\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"AUC decay curve, 但需标注 rewrite mode inflation warning\"\n    analysis: >\n      在 worst-case 下此实验仅定位为 feasibility pilot。CI 虽然 robust（lower=0.6859），但\n      rewrite mode 的 cross-model transfer 差（61-63%）意味着 K*=2 的泛化性完全依赖 continuation\n      mode 实验。如果 continuation mode 边界案例（Qwen-cont CI lower=0.6015）被质疑，mvp-001\n      无法提供 backup。\n\n  - name: \"Pythia-1.4B C4 Depth Chain\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: \"Pythia-1.4B, nucleus p=0.95 T=1.0, C4 5K docs, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 2\n      auc_0v1: 0.9932\n      auc_1v2: 0.6539\n      auc_2v3: 0.5515\n      ci_1v2_lower: 0.6454\n      jsd_0v1: 0.2142\n      jsd_1v2: 0.014\n      ordinal_accuracy: 0.383\n    result_rationale: >\n      Pythia K*=2 on C4 是相对稳健的数据点（CI lower=0.6454, +4.5pp above θ），worst-case 下\n      仍然成立。但审稿人会指出 Pythia 是 The Pile 训练的旧架构（GPT-NeoX），与现代 decoder-only\n      架构（LLaMA/Qwen/Mistral）差异大，代表性有限。Ordinal accuracy 仅 38.3%（6-class random=16.7%）\n      被认为 \"marginally better than random on fine-grained depth\"，进一步削弱 practical value 叙事。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Pairwise AUC with bootstrap CI\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"JSD cliff plot showing 0v1→1v2 drop\"\n    analysis: >\n      Pythia C4 K*=2 在 worst-case 下是最不被质疑的 C4 data point 之一（margin +4.5pp）。\n      但 ordinal accuracy ~38% 加上 K*≤3 的 trivial 质疑，审稿人可能认为 \"Pythia generates\n      poor text → K*=2 simply means the text is too distinguishable at gen-1 but collapses\n      to noise at gen-2\"，将 K*=2 归因于 model weakness 而非 domain property。\n\n  - name: \"OLMo-1B C4 Depth Chain\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: \"OLMo-1B, nucleus p=0.95 T=1.0, C4 5K docs, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 2\n      auc_0v1: 0.997\n      auc_1v2: 0.6146\n      auc_2v3: 0.5497\n      ci_1v2_lower: 0.6045\n      jsd_0v1: 0.2394\n      jsd_1v2: 0.0130\n      ordinal_accuracy: 0.3685\n    result_rationale: >\n      OLMo CI lower=0.6045 仅 +0.45pp above θ=0.60——在 worst-case 下审稿人将其标记为 \"borderline\n      pass, θ-dependent\"。如果 θ 从 0.60 上调至 0.61 或 0.62（审稿人认为合理的 sensitivity test），\n      OLMo 立即变为 K*=1。这使得 8/9 K*=2 claim 退化为 7/9 或更少。OLMo 是 1B 模型，被归类为\n      \"small model that doesn't generate very well\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Pairwise AUC, OLMo row highlighted as borderline\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"θ-sensitivity plot showing OLMo flips at θ≈0.605\"\n    analysis: >\n      OLMo 是 worst-case 下的 soft vulnerability：CI lower 几乎踩线，θ-sensitivity 下很容易翻转。\n      审稿人如果要求 θ=0.65 作为 \"meaningful effect size\"，OLMo 和 Qwen-cont 都会变 K*=1，\n      C4 从 8/9 K*=2 降至 6/9，narrative 从 \"dominant mode\" 退化为 \"slight majority\"。\n\n  - name: \"Qwen-7B C4 Cross-Scale\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-7B, C4 5K docs, depth 0-5, scorer=Qwen2.5-1.5B\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 2\n      auc_0v1: 0.9644\n      auc_1v2: 0.6178\n      auc_2v3: 0.5460\n      ci_1v2_lower: 0.6079\n      ci_2v3_upper: 0.5594\n    result_rationale: >\n      Qwen-7B C4 K*=2 成立（CI lower=0.6079, +0.79pp），但 margin 较小。Worst-case 下审稿人\n      注意到 0v1 AUC=0.9644 远低于小模型（Pythia 0.9932, OLMo 0.997），说明 7B 模型生成的 gen-1\n      文本已经更接近 human text——这意味着更大模型的 0v1 区分度在下降。审稿人可能推断 \"70B+ models\n      would have even lower 0v1 AUC, and 1v2 would drop below θ, making K*=1 the norm\n      at scale\"，直接挑战 scale generalization。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Scale comparison (1.5B vs 7B vs 14B) with 0v1 trend\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"0v1 AUC vs model scale plot showing declining trend\"\n    analysis: >\n      7B scale 确认 K*=2 但暴露了 scale-dependent 0v1 decline trend。Worst-case 下审稿人\n      据此论证 \"K*=2 is a small-model artifact; at frontier scale, even 0v1 detection\n      will become unreliable\"。14B (AUC 0v1=0.9598) 延续下降趋势，加剧此担忧。\n\n  - name: \"LLaMA-8B C4 Cross-Family\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-018\"\n    description: \"LLaMA-3.1-8B, continuation mode, C4 5K docs, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 2\n      auc_0v1: 0.9225\n      auc_1v2: 0.6123\n      auc_2v3: 0.5274\n      ci_1v2_lower: 0.6028\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLaMA-8B CI lower=0.6028 仅 +0.28pp above θ——worst-case 下这是 C4 实验中最脆弱的 K*=2\n      判定。0v1 AUC=0.9225 是所有 C4 模型中最低的，说明 LLaMA 生成的 gen-1 文本最接近 human。\n      审稿人直接指出 \"LLaMA-8B is already at the margin; LLaMA-70B would almost certainly\n      fall below θ\"。加上 cross-scorer 使用 Qwen-1.5B（不同家族、不同 tokenizer），信号衰减\n      是预期中的——但审稿人可能认为这是 scorer inadequacy 而非 genuine K*=2。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: LLaMA row with CI callout\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"CI forest plot with LLaMA near θ boundary\"\n    analysis: >\n      LLaMA-8B 是 worst-case 下 C4 K*=2 的最薄弱环节。CI lower=0.6028 意味着在 bootstrap\n      的 2.5th percentile 仅以 0.28pp 过关。任何关于 θ 选择的质疑都能翻转此结果。审稿人会指出\n      LLaMA 系列是当前最广泛使用的开源模型，如果其 K*=2 不稳健，实践价值大打折扣。\n\n  - name: \"Mistral-7B C4 Cross-Family\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-019\"\n    description: \"Mistral-7B-v0.3, continuation mode, C4 5K docs, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 1\n      auc_0v1: 0.9843\n      auc_1v2: 0.5935\n      auc_2v3: 0.5402\n      ci_1v2_lower: 0.5835\n      ci_1v2_upper: 0.6032\n      p_auc_leq_060: 0.9017\n    result_rationale: >\n      Mistral C4 K*=1 是已确认的 one-wash case。CI upper=0.6032 勉强触及 θ（P(AUC≤0.60)=90%），\n      cross-scorer 进一步降至 0.5695。Worst-case 下审稿人将 Mistral K*=1 与 LLaMA/OLMo/Qwen-cont\n      的 borderline K*=2 放在一起，论证 \"the real pattern is K*=1 for most modern models on\n      C4, with a few models barely crossing a conveniently chosen threshold\"。这直接攻击\n      8/9 K*=2 的 claim——如果 θ 上调 0.03pp，变为 5/9 K*=1。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Mistral C4 vs arXiv contrast row\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"AUC distribution plot highlighting Mistral as K*=1 outlier on C4\"\n    analysis: >\n      Mistral K*=1 on C4 but K*=3 on arXiv 是 domain dependence 的最强证据——这一点在\n      worst-case 下仍然成立且是唯一的 bright spot。但审稿人可能 reframe：Mistral 在 C4 上\n      K*=1 恰好说明 one-wash 是 more common than claimed，且与 Qwen-cont（CI lower=0.6015）\n      和 LLaMA（0.6028）合并看，C4 的 \"dominant K*=2\" 叙事站不住。\n\n  - name: \"Qwen-1.5B-Instruct Continuation Mode\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-017\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct continuation mode, C4 5K docs, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 2\n      auc_0v1: 0.9972\n      auc_1v2: 0.6114\n      auc_2v3: 0.5609\n      ci_1v2_lower: 0.6015\n      jsd_0v1: 0.2863\n      jsd_1v2: 0.0051\n    result_rationale: >\n      CI lower=0.6015 仅 +0.15pp above θ——这是 C4 所有 K*=2 判定中最边缘的。Worst-case 下\n      审稿人指出 cross-scorer validation (exp_A_alt_scorer) 中 Qwen-cont 被 Pythia 评分时\n      K*=1（AUC 1v2=0.5923），证明 K*=2 依赖于 same-family scorer。论文声称 scorer independence\n      但最边缘的 case 恰好在 cross-scorer 下 fail，这在审稿人看来是 \"selective reporting\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Qwen-cont same-scorer vs cross-scorer comparison\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"CI error bar plot with θ line, Qwen-cont nearly touching\"\n    analysis: >\n      Qwen-cont 是 worst-case 下的 Achilles heel。CI lower=0.6015 + cross-scorer K*=1\n      组合直接威胁 \"8/9 K*=2\" 的核心叙事。审稿人完全有理由要求 cross-scorer 作为 canonical\n      condition，此时 C4 K*=2 从 8/9 变为 ≤7/9（OLMo cross-scorer 未明确测试但预期也边缘），\n      且最边缘的几个 data points 全部依赖 θ=0.60。\n\n  - name: \"Qwen-1.5B Base Model C4\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-016\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-1.5B base continuation mode, C4 5K docs, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 2\n      auc_0v1: 0.987\n      auc_1v2: 0.6262\n      auc_2v3: 0.5496\n      ci_1v2_lower: 0.6168\n    result_rationale: >\n      Base model CI lower=0.6168（+1.7pp above θ）比 Instruct 更稳健。但 worst-case 下审稿人\n      注意到 base vs instruct 差异不显著（CI overlap），质疑 \"if base and instruct give the\n      same K*, what does this say about the generality of the finding?\" 结论是 K*=2\n      对 alignment 不敏感——这本身可以是正面发现，但在 worst-case framing 下被审稿人忽略。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Base vs Instruct comparison\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Base model 是 C4 上相对安全的 data point（margin +1.7pp）。Worst-case 下不是攻击重点，\n      但也不增加额外信息——审稿人认为 base/instruct 不影响 K* 是 \"expected, not interesting\"。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # C1' Domain Ablation — Wikipedia\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Wikipedia Domain Ablation (Qwen-1.5B)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-023\"\n    description: \"Wikipedia seed, Qwen2.5-1.5B base, continuation, 5K docs, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 2\n      auc_1v2: 0.6193\n      auc_2v3: 0.5498\n      note: \"same-family scorer; cross-scorer controls reduce to K*=1\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Qwen self-scorer 给 Wiki K*=2，但 D060 cross-family scorer（Pythia）证实 K*=1。\n      Worst-case 下审稿人将此视为 scorer confound 的 poster child：\"your own analysis shows\n      same-family scoring inflates K* by +1 on Wikipedia, yet you report K*=2 in the\n      same table as other models?\" 论文虽然在正文报 scorer-controlled K*=1，但审稿人质疑\n      为什么需要额外实验来发现这个问题——暗示其他域也可能有未检测到的 confound。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Wiki K* with scorer confound annotation\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scorer confound illustration: same-family vs cross-family\"\n    analysis: >\n      Wiki K*=1 在 scorer control 后是 robust 的（6 models all K*=1）。但 worst-case 下\n      scorer confound 的 existence 本身成为攻击向量：审稿人质疑 \"if you need cross-family\n      scoring to get correct K* on Wikipedia, how do you know C4 K*=2 isn't also inflated?\"\n      这迫使论文对每个 domain×model 组合都做 cross-scorer validation——资源约束下无法完成。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # C1' Domain Ablation — arXiv\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"arXiv Domain Ablation (Qwen-1.5B)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-024\"\n    description: \"arXiv abstracts, Qwen2.5-1.5B base, continuation, 5K docs, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 3\n      auc_0v1: 0.9946\n      auc_1v2: 0.858\n      auc_2v3: 0.6427\n      ci_2v3_lower: 0.6275\n      jsd_0v1: 0.171\n      jsd_1v2: 0.057\n      jsd_2v3: 0.020\n    result_rationale: >\n      arXiv K*=3 是 worst-case 下最稳健的发现：5/5 domain-competent models 一致，CI margin\n      充足（+2.75pp）。但审稿人会质疑：\"arXiv abstracts 是高度结构化的专业文本，current LLMs\n      生成的 arXiv 文本质量低（citation hallucination, formula errors），K*=3 可能仅反映\n      生成质量差而非 domain structural complexity。\" 另外 arXiv 在 web 污染场景中不是主要\n      concern——审稿人认为 \"who cares about arXiv K*=3 when the real problem is web text?\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: arXiv pairwise AUC across 5 models\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"arXiv vs C4 JSD cliff comparison\"\n    analysis: >\n      arXiv K*=3 在 worst-case 下从 \"domain hierarchy crown jewel\" 变为 \"niche finding\n      with limited practical relevance\"。审稿人承认它 cross-validated 但认为 practical\n      implications 弱（谁在 curate arXiv data?），且 K*=3 vs K*=2 的差异仅一步——\n      \"so structured text resists one more pass, is that really a paper?\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # C1' Decoding & Robustness\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Decoding Strategy Ablation (Qwen-1.5B)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-1.5B: greedy/nucleus p=0.9/T=0.7/T=1.2, C4 5K, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star_all_configs: 2\n      auc_1v2_range: [0.6862, 0.7037]\n      auc_1v2_greedy: 0.6892\n      auc_1v2_nuc09: 0.6862\n      auc_1v2_t07: 0.6885\n      auc_1v2_t12: 0.7037\n      note: \"nuc09 2v3 CI upper=0.601 crosses θ\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      4 种解码策略均 K*=2，但 nuc09 的 2v3 CI upper=0.601 几乎触及 θ，暗示 K*=3 在某些\n      decoding 下 borderline 可能。Worst-case 下审稿人承认 K* 对 decoding 不变，但指出\n      \"decoding invariance is expected — all strategies sample from the same distribution,\n      temperature merely scales logits. This is not a surprising finding.\" 实验成功但\n      不增加 novelty。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: 4 decoding × pairwise AUC matrix\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Decoding strategy comparison bar chart\"\n    analysis: >\n      Decoding invariance 在 worst-case 下被视为 \"sanity check, not contribution\"。\n      审稿人不会因此扣分但也不加分。唯一风险：nuc09 2v3 borderline 被拿来支撑 \"K* boundary\n      is fuzzy and θ-dependent\" 的论点。\n\n  - name: \"Pythia-1.4B Decoding Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-020\"\n    description: \"Pythia-1.4B: greedy/nuc09/T=0.7/T=1.2, C4 5K, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star_all_configs: 2\n      auc_1v2_greedy: 0.8838\n      auc_1v2_nuc09: 0.677\n      auc_1v2_t07: 0.7265\n      auc_1v2_t12: 0.6172\n    result_rationale: >\n      Pythia greedy 1v2=0.8838 异常高——因为 Pythia greedy 产生大量重复文本（repetition collapse），\n      创造了 artificial depth signal。Worst-case 下审稿人将此作为 \"your features capture\n      degeneracy, not depth\" 的证据。T=1.2（高温）AUC=0.6172 最低，接近 θ——审稿人指出\n      \"higher temperature narrows the depth signal gap, suggesting depth discrimination\n      is partly a temperature artifact\"。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Pythia decoding comparison with greedy anomaly flagged\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Pythia decoding 在 worst-case 下暴露了 feature sensitivity to text degeneracy。\n      Greedy 的 0.88 被攻击为 \"measuring repetition, not depth\"，T=1.2 的 0.62 被用来\n      论证 \"depth signal vanishes with sufficient randomness\"。K* 仍为 2 但可信度受损。\n\n  - name: \"Text Length Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-021\"\n    description: \"Qwen continuation, 128/256/512 tokens, C4 5K, depth 0-5\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star_128: 2\n      k_star_256: 2\n      k_star_512: 2\n      auc_1v2_128: 0.6219\n      auc_1v2_256: 0.6282\n      auc_1v2_512: 0.6073\n      ci_512_1v2_lower: 0.5979\n      ci_512_1v2_verdict: BORDERLINE\n    result_rationale: >\n      512 token 条件 CI lower=0.5979 < θ=0.60——worst-case 下审稿人指出 \"at 512 tokens,\n      which is a realistic document length, K*=2 already fails bootstrap CI. Your\n      K*=2 finding is an artifact of short (128-256 token) text segments.\" 这直接威胁\n      ecological validity：真实文档通常远超 256 tokens，而 K*=2 在更长文本上不稳健。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Length × K* with 512-token CI flagged\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"AUC vs length curve showing 512-token drop\"\n    analysis: >\n      Length ablation 的 512-token borderline failure 是 worst-case 下的关键攻击点。\n      审稿人论证 \"if K*=2 only holds for short snippets, the practical applicability\n      to real-world document-level contamination detection is limited\"。这与 C3 的 negative\n      results 形成共振——方法论和实践价值同时被质疑。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # C1' Cross-Model Transfer & Scorer Independence\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cross-Model Transfer 4×4 Matrix\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-013\"\n    description: \"4 generators × 4 scorers transfer accuracy matrix\"\n    expected_results:\n      pythia_olmo_retention: \"91-92%\"\n      qwen_cont_others_retention: \"80-85%\"\n      qwen_rw_others_retention: \"61-63%\"\n      0v1_cross_all_above: 0.96\n      within_avg_pw_auc: 0.6099\n      cross_avg_pw_auc: 0.5905\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cross-model transfer 80-92% 是正面结果，但 worst-case 下审稿人注意到：\n      (1) Qwen-rewrite 跨模型仅 61-63%——generation mode 是比 model identity 更大的 confound；\n      (2) Cross average pw_auc=0.5905 < θ=0.60——跨模型平均辨别力不足以支撑 K*=2；\n      (3) 0v1 >0.96 说明 binary detection 已解决，fine-grained depth 不增加实践价值。\n      审稿人结论：\"binary contamination detection transfers perfectly; depth estimation\n      does not add practical value over binary.\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: 4×4 transfer matrix (accuracy and tau)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Transfer heatmap with within vs cross diagonal comparison\"\n    analysis: >\n      Transfer 实验在 worst-case 下产生 double-edged 结论：binary (0v1) 完美迁移→\n      既有 binary detectors 足够；fine-grained depth 迁移下降→depth estimation 不实用。\n      审稿人可能总结 \"the transferable signal is exactly what binary detectors already capture.\"\n\n  - name: \"4×4 Cross-Scorer Matrix\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-022\"\n    description: \"4 generators × 4 scorers, K* scorer independence\"\n    expected_results:\n      k2_count: 11\n      k1_count: 1\n      exception: \"qwen_cont256×pythia (1v2=0.5979, K*=1)\"\n      scorer_delta_max: 0.025\n    result_rationale: >\n      11/12 K*=2 看似稳健，但 worst-case 下审稿人关注：(1) 唯一 K*=1 case 恰好是\n      Qwen-cont（论文最边缘 case）被 Pythia score——证实 cross-scorer 下 Qwen-cont 不稳健；\n      (2) 此 matrix 基于 Pythia-greedy（1v2~0.88 repetition collapse）和 Qwen-base/cont，\n      不包含 Mistral/LLaMA 作为 generator，覆盖不完整；(3) cross_scorer_kstar_preservation_rate\n      下降至 0.65-0.75 range（worst-case 指标范围），如果扩展到所有 domain×model 组合。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Cross-scorer K* matrix\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-scorer 在 worst-case 下从 \"11/12 confirms K*=2\" 变为 \"the one failure\n      happens to be the most critical case (Qwen-cont), and the matrix doesn't include\n      the models most likely to fail (Mistral, LLaMA).\" 审稿人要求 full coverage 的\n      cross-scorer matrix（~30 combos for 4 domains × all models）——资源不可能满足。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # C1' Feature & Method Validation\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Feature Group Ablation & Degradation Ordering\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: \"Per feature group pairwise AUC and saturation depth analysis\"\n    expected_results:\n      cross_model_spearman_rho: \">0.85\"\n      shared_top_discriminators: \"surp_d1_std, surp_std, surp_d2_std\"\n      limitation_1v2_weakness: \"τ~0.37 at 1v2 pair\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Feature ordering 跨模型 ρ>0.85 是正面结果，但 worst-case 下审稿人指出 1v2 pair 的\n      cross-model consistency 最弱（τ~0.37）——而 1v2 恰好是决定 K*=2 vs K*=1 的 boundary pair。\n      \"The one depth pair that matters most for your K* determination has the weakest\n      cross-model feature agreement.\" 加之 features 是 \"standard text statistics\n      (surprisal, entropy, etc.)\"，审稿人质疑 \"15D feature engineering is not a methodological\n      contribution; these are well-known text quality metrics repurposed.\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Feature ranking comparison across models\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Degradation ordering heatmap\"\n    analysis: >\n      Feature ablation 在 worst-case 下被降级为 \"expected results with known metrics\"。\n      1v2 inconsistency 被放大为 methodology weakness。审稿人总结 \"feature engineering\n      adds nothing new; surprisal-based features have been used in MGT detection since 2023.\"\n\n  - name: \"Bootstrap CI & Permutation Tests\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: \"θ sensitivity at 0.55/0.60/0.65/0.70 with bootstrap CI and permutation\"\n    expected_results:\n      all_1v2_ci_lower_above_060: true\n      most_marginal: \"Qwen-cont CI lower=0.6015 (+0.15pp)\"\n      theta_060_k2_count: \"8/9\"\n      theta_065_k2_count: \"~5/9\"\n      theta_070_k2_count: \"~2/9\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      θ-sensitivity 在 worst-case 下是审稿人的主要攻击工具：θ=0.60 下 8/9 K*=2，但\n      θ=0.65 下降至约 5/9，θ=0.70 下仅约 2/9。审稿人指出 \"Cohen's h=0.20 (θ=0.60) is\n      conventionally 'small effect size' — your K*=2 claim literally rests on a 'small'\n      effect. At 'medium' effect (h=0.50, θ≈0.73), virtually all models show K*=1.\"\n      Qwen-cont 的 +0.15pp margin 被视为 cherry-picked threshold 的典型证据。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: K* at multiple θ values\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"K* vs θ sensitivity curve for all models\"\n    analysis: >\n      θ-sensitivity 是 worst-case 的核心弱点之一。审稿人可以合理要求 θ=0.65 作为\n      minimum \"practically meaningful\" threshold，此时 K*=2 的 dominant mode claim 崩塌。\n      论文的 permutation test 只证明 AUC ≠ 0.50（非随机），不证明 AUC 达到 \"meaningful\" 水平。\n      Cohen's h=0.20 defense 在 ML 社区不如在心理学中 convincing。\n\n  - name: \"Neural Probe (Learned Representations)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-015\"\n    description: \"Frozen embeddings + MLP vs 15D features across 3 models\"\n    expected_results:\n      pythia_k_neural: 2\n      olmo_k_neural: 2\n      qwen_k_neural: 3\n      key: \"Neural K* is model-dependent (Qwen=3 only under self-scorer)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Neural probe 本应证明 \"K*=2 is representation-intrinsic\"，但结果 model-dependent：\n      Qwen self-scorer K*_neural=3 > K*_15D=2，而 Pythia/OLMo K*_neural=2 = K*_15D。\n      Worst-case 下审稿人解读为 \"the neural probe shows that richer representations can\n      extract more depth signal (K*=3 for Qwen), meaning your 15D features are a\n      lossy bottleneck that artificially caps K* at 2. K*=2 is a feature engineering\n      artifact, not a data-intrinsic boundary.\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Neural probe vs 15D K* comparison\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Neural probe 的 model-dependent K* 在 worst-case 下直接反驳 \"K*=2 is data-intrinsic\"\n      的 claim。如果 Qwen neural probe 达到 K*=3，说明 information exists at depth 2v3\n      但 15D features 太粗糙无法捕获。审稿人总结：\"your K* is a property of your measurement\n      apparatus, not the data.\" 论文将此 reframe 为 \"model-free features give consistent K*\"\n      的 practical advantage，但审稿人不买账。\n\n  - name: \"Ordinal vs Multinomial vs Regression Baselines\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: \"CORAL ordinal vs multiclass LightGBM vs ordinal logistic regression\"\n    expected_results:\n      obd_lgbm_best_acc: 0.4229\n      multiclass_lgbm_acc: 0.4182\n      ordinal_logreg_acc: 0.3636\n      obd_vs_multiclass_delta: \"+0.47pp\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      OBD-LightGBM 仅比 multiclass LightGBM 好 0.47pp accuracy（42.3% vs 41.8%），\n      ordinal structure 的 advantage 微乎其微。Worst-case 下审稿人指出 \"ordinal modeling\n      adds complexity without meaningful improvement; a simple multiclass classifier\n      performs nearly identically, undermining the claim that depth has ordinal structure\n      worth exploiting.\" 此外所有方法 accuracy < 43%（6-class，random=16.7%），绝对\n      performance 不 impressive。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: 3 methods × 3 models comparison\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Ordinal baseline 在 worst-case 下证明 ordinal structure 几乎无 practical benefit。\n      审稿人将此与 C3 negative results 联系：\"even your ordinal classifier barely beats\n      multiclass, and your K*-aware filtering barely beats binary — the ordinal/depth\n      information has no actionable value.\"\n\n  - name: \"LLM Zero-Shot Depth Estimation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: \"GPT-5.5 / Claude Opus 4.6 zero-shot depth estimation, 500 samples\"\n    expected_results:\n      gpt55_5class_acc: 0.332\n      claude_5class_acc: 0.331\n      odb_baseline_acc: 0.386\n      binary_acc_both: \"~88%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Frontier LLMs 5-class accuracy ~33% < OBD 38.6%——看似证明需要专门方法。但 worst-case\n      下审稿人指出：(1) 33% vs 38.6% 差距不大（McNemar p>0.05 不显著），不能 claim OBD\n      \"significantly outperforms\"；(2) binary 88% 说明 depth-0 detection 已被 LLM 解决，\n      而 fine-grained depth 对所有方法（包括 OBD）都失败——\"your method is slightly better\n      at a task nobody can do well\"；(3) 500 samples 太少（power concerns）。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: LLM vs OBD accuracy comparison\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-depth accuracy breakdown showing all methods fail at depth 1-4\"\n    analysis: >\n      LLM baseline 在 worst-case 下被 turned against the paper：\"all methods fail at\n      fine-grained depth estimation, including yours. The task as defined may be\n      fundamentally too hard to be useful.\" Binary detection at 88% 强化 \"just do binary\"\n      的审稿人立场。\n\n  - name: \"Binary Detector Confidence as Depth Proxy\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-012\"\n    description: \"DivEye/Binoculars score Spearman correlation with true depth\"\n    expected_results:\n      binary_kstar: 1\n      obd_kstar: 2\n      max_spearman_rho: 0.46\n      six_class_acc_max: 0.199\n    result_rationale: >\n      Binary detectors K*=1 vs OBD K*=2 的差异证明深度信息超越 binary。但 worst-case 下\n      审稿人质疑：\"OBD uses 15 hand-crafted features and a trained classifier, while\n      DivEye/Binoculars are single-score methods designed for binary detection — the\n      comparison is unfair. A fair comparison would train a classifier on DivEye features\n      across depth levels.\" 6-class accuracy ≤19.9% 再次证明 fine-grained depth 对所有方法\n      都不 work。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Binary vs OBD comparison\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Non-monotonic AUC plot for binary detectors\"\n    analysis: >\n      Binary detector comparison 在 worst-case 下被视为 \"strawman baseline\"——用单分数\n      binary 工具对比 15D trained classifier 不公平。审稿人可能要求与 \"binary detector\n      features + depth-aware classifier\" 对比。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # C1' Retrain Chain & Ecological Validity\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Retrain Chain (Pythia-1.4B)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: \"Pythia-1.4B LoRA retrain chain, C4 5K, depth 0-4\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: \">=4\"\n      auc_0v1: 0.9847\n      auc_1v2: 0.9484\n      auc_2v3: 0.8888\n      auc_3v4: 0.7982\n    result_rationale: >\n      Retrain K*≥4 大幅超越 prompt-chain K*=2——但 worst-case 下审稿人认为 \"retrain-chain\n      detects LoRA adaptation artifacts, not text-intrinsic depth signal. K*≥4 is an\n      artifact of your experimental setup, not a property of recursive contamination.\"\n      更重要的是，retrain chain 与 prompt chain 的 K* 差距（2 vs ≥4）反而证明 K* depends\n      heavily on the contamination mechanism，而论文只测了一种 mechanism (prompt-chain)——\n      ecological validity concern 加剧。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Prompt-chain vs retrain-chain AUC comparison\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"K* divergence between contamination mechanisms\"\n    analysis: >\n      Retrain chain 在 worst-case 下从 \"ecological validity evidence\" 变为 \"evidence\n      of mechanism-dependence\"。审稿人论证 K*=2 只是 prompt-chain specific，真实世界\n      可能有 K*=7（retrain）或 K*=1（其他机制），论文的 K*=2 claim 无法泛化。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # C1' Additional Robustness\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Subsampling Power Curve\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-028\"\n    description: \"C4 subsampling n={1000,...,5000} × 10 resamples\"\n    expected_results:\n      min_n_100pct: 2000\n      n1000_rate: 0.3\n      n2000_rate: 1.0\n      n5000_auc: 0.6288\n    result_rationale: >\n      n≥2000 给 100% detection——但 worst-case 下审稿人指出 \"the fact that you need n=2000\n      samples to reliably detect K*=2 means the effect size is tiny. For comparison,\n      binary detection (0v1) works with n=100. This confirms K*=2 is a statistical\n      artifact visible only in aggregate, not a practically useful signal for individual\n      documents.\" n=1000 仅 30% detection rate 强化 \"weak signal\" 叙事。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Power curve with detection rates\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Power curve plot\"\n    analysis: >\n      Power curve 在 worst-case 下被 used against the paper：大样本需求 = 小效应量 = \n      不实用。审稿人对比 binary detection 的 near-perfect per-sample accuracy 与 depth\n      estimation 的 n=2000 aggregate requirement。\n\n  - name: \"LaTeX Markup Removal Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-027\"\n    description: \"arXiv text with LaTeX stripped, verify K*=3 preserved\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star_preserved: true\n      auc_2v3_original: 0.6436\n      auc_2v3_stripped: 0.6229\n      delta_2v3: -0.021\n    result_rationale: >\n      K*=3 after LaTeX removal is positive——但 worst-case 下 2v3 AUC 从 0.6436 降至 0.6229\n      （-2.1pp），margin 从 +4.3pp 收窄至 +2.3pp above θ。审稿人指出 \"LaTeX removal costs\n      you nearly half your safety margin. What about other formatting artifacts (citation\n      brackets, equation numbering, section headers)? Full markup removal might push\n      2v3 below θ.\" 实验被视为 incomplete ablation。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Original vs stripped AUC\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      LaTeX ablation 在 worst-case 下 partially succeeds 但暴露 format-dependency：\n      LaTeX 贡献了 ~2pp 的 signal，更彻底的 stripping 可能消除剩余 margin。审稿人要求\n      full-structure removal ablation（headers, citations, formulas 全部 normalize），\n      这个实验未做。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # C3 Filtering Experiments\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Downstream Filtering Evaluation (Qwen, C4)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: \"6 strategies × 5 seeds, continued pretraining, MMLU+HellaSwag\"\n    expected_results:\n      binary_ours_mmlu: \"0.5941±0.0008\"\n      no_filter_mmlu: \"0.5865±0.0010\"\n      delta_mmlu: \"+0.0076\"\n      delta_hellaswag: \"+0.0063\"\n      best_strategy: \"binary-ours\"\n      graduated_a09_mmlu: \"0.5892±0.0008\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Binary outperforms all——但 worst-case 下审稿人质疑：(1) 所有策略都 degrade vs\n      base model（0.6018 MMLU），\"your best filtering still makes the model worse than\n      doing nothing\"；(2) binary vs no_filter delta=0.76pp MMLU——统计显著但 practically\n      meaningless；(3) graduated α monotone increasing 说明 \"more filtering is always\n      better regardless of depth awareness\"——K* information 没有 incremental value over\n      simple quality threshold；(4) DSIR 差于 no_filter，说明 distribution matching 反而有害，\n      但这是 DSIR 的问题不是本文的贡献。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: All 6 strategies × MMLU/HellaSwag\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Strategy ranking bar chart\"\n    analysis: >\n      C3 在 worst-case 下的叙事崩塌：binary beats graduated（不符合 \"depth-aware curation\n      is better\" 的 hypothesis），所有策略 < base model，delta < 1pp。审稿人总结 \"K*\n      provides no curation benefit beyond what a simple binary classifier already gives.\"\n      c3_binary_vs_nofilter_hellaswag_delta_pp 在 3.8-6.1pp range（dose response 中），\n      但单个 30% ratio 下仅 ~6pp——不足以 justify depth estimation pipeline 的复杂性。\n\n  - name: \"Contamination Dose-Response\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: \"10%/30%/50% contamination ratio × 3 strategies × 5 seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      binary_advantage_hellaswag_10pct: \"+0.38pp\"\n      binary_advantage_hellaswag_30pct: \"+0.61pp\"\n      binary_advantage_hellaswag_50pct: \"+0.51pp\"\n      graduated_vs_nofilter: \"identical at all ratios\"\n      all_p_values_hellaswag: \"≤0.004\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Binary filtering 在所有 ratio 下显著优于 no_filter（HellaSwag），但 graduated = no_filter\n      在所有 ratio 下完全一致。Worst-case 下这是 C3 的 death blow：dose-response 本应展示\n      \"as contamination increases, depth-aware filtering becomes more important\"，实际结果是\n      \"graduated filtering provides zero benefit at any contamination level\"。审稿人结论：\n      \"binary filtering works because it removes synthetic text; the depth dimension K* adds\n      nothing. Your headline claim C3 is falsified by your own dose-response analysis.\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: 3 ratios × 3 strategies with p-values\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dose-response curve with graduated=no_filter overlap\"\n    analysis: >\n      Dose-response 在 worst-case 下完全否定 C3 的 depth-aware curation hypothesis。\n      Binary 的优势仅来自 \"remove synthetic text\" 而非 \"use depth information\"。\n      审稿人会质疑论文的 claim rewrite——如果 C3 只是 \"binary filtering works\"，这已被\n      Drayson et al. (2025) 证明，不是新贡献。\n\n  - name: \"Pythia-1.4B Filtering Replication\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-025\"\n    description: \"Pythia LoRA rank=8, 3 strategies × 3 seeds, MMLU+HellaSwag\"\n    expected_results:\n      binary_ours_mmlu: \"0.2585±0.0004\"\n      no_filter_mmlu: \"0.2568±0.0012\"\n      delta_max: \"0.0017 (noise)\"\n      conclusion: \"negative — all strategies identical\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Pythia filtering 完全 negative：三种策略 within noise（max delta 0.17pp MMLU）。\n      Worst-case 下审稿人直接 quote：\"your filtering experiment fails to replicate on a\n      second model, suggesting the Qwen result (exp-006) is model-specific.\" C3 的 scope\n      从 \"general principle\" 退化为 \"works on Qwen-1.5B with C4 data only\"——太窄无法\n      作为 conference contribution。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Pythia filtering negative result\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Pythia negative result 在 worst-case 下彻底瓦解 C3 的 generalizability。Qwen exp-006\n      可能是 model-specific artifact（Qwen-1.5B 的特定 tokenizer/architecture 恰好对\n      binary filtering 敏感）。审稿人不会接受 \"C3 validated for one model configuration\"\n      作为 conference contribution。\n\n  - name: \"arXiv Graduated vs Binary Filtering\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-026\"\n    description: \"arXiv depth chain (K*=3), 3 strategies × 5 seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      graduated_mmlu: \"0.5900±0.0011\"\n      binary_mmlu: \"0.5876±0.0004\"\n      no_filter_mmlu: \"0.5899±0.0008\"\n      conclusion: \"negative — all identical\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      arXiv K*=3 是 C3 的关键测试场——如果 K*=3 则 graduated 应优于 binary（depth 3 信息\n      有增量价值）。结果完全 negative。Worst-case 下这是最致命的 C3 failure：唯一一个\n      K*>2 的域上，depth-aware filtering 仍然无效。审稿人总结 \"K* characterization (C1')\n      and practical curation (C3) are disconnected — knowing K* doesn't help you curate\n      data better.\" 这直接攻击论文的 motivation：\"why measure K* if it has no downstream\n      utility?\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: arXiv 3 strategies × MMLU/HellaSwag\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      arXiv filtering negative 是 worst-case 下的致命证据。Paper 的 story spine 声称\n      \"domain-dependent K* provides actionable curation guidance\"，但 K*=3 域上的 curation\n      完全无效。审稿人在 C3 上的 verdict 将是 \"insufficient practical contribution\"——\n      与 worst-case 核心假设完全一致。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # C2 Methodology & Baselines\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Naturalistic Validation (Common Crawl)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-014\"\n    description: \"Common Crawl 2025/2026 snapshot depth prediction + correlation\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"planned/not_executed\"\n      predicted_spearman_with_alignscore: [0.15, 0.30]\n      predicted_spearman_with_vocab_richness: [0.20, 0.35]\n      predicted_depth_distribution_mode: 0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst-case 下此实验未执行或结果令人失望：(1) Common Crawl 样本的 predicted depth\n      分布高度偏向 depth 0（大部分 web 文本仍为 human-written），缺少 depth>1 的 ground\n      truth 验证；(2) 与 AlignScore 的 correlation 微弱（ρ~0.15-0.30）——depth 预测\n      与独立质量指标不一致；(3) 无法验证 K* boundary 在 wild data 上是否成立（无 ground\n      truth depth labels）。审稿人标注为 \"critical missing experiment for ecological validity\"。\n      如果已执行，低 correlation 被解读为 \"your lab-measured K* doesn't transfer to real-world\n      contamination patterns.\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Predicted depth distribution (if executed)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Depth prediction histogram of CC samples\"\n    analysis: >\n      Naturalistic validation 缺失或失败在 worst-case 下是审稿人的主要 concern：\"all\n      your experiments are in controlled lab settings with clean prompt-chains. You\n      have zero evidence this works on real-world contaminated data.\" 即使执行了，低\n      correlation + 缺少 ground truth 也无法消除质疑。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Code Domain — RUNNING experiments (worst-case predictions)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Code Domain — Mistral-7B (RUNNING, worst-case prediction)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_code_mistral7b\"\n    description: \"Mistral-7B Code/Python depth chain, predicted K*=1\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 1\n      auc_0v1: [0.91, 0.95]\n      auc_1v2: [0.52, 0.58]\n      auc_2v3: [0.50, 0.53]\n      ci_1v2_upper: [0.55, 0.60]\n      jsd_1v2: [0.003, 0.006]\n    result_rationale: >\n      Mistral C4 已是 K*=1（AUC 1v2=0.5935），Code domain 对 Mistral 更不利：Mistral 的\n      code generation 能力虽优于 Pythia 但仍低于 Qwen/LLaMA code-tuned 变体。Code domain\n      的 syntactic regularity（indentation, brackets, keywords）使 Mistral 的 code 生成\n      快速 converge 到 template-like patterns，1v2 信号在一次迭代后即消失。AUC 1v2 预期\n      0.52-0.58，低于 C4 的 0.5935——Code 的强结构约束加速了信息丧失。Cross-family scorer\n      (Qwen) 可能进一步降低 AUC（如 C4 上 Mistral cross-scorer 从 0.5935 降至 0.5695）。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Code domain cross-model K* summary with Mistral=1\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Mistral Code K*=1 在 worst-case 下意味着 Code ceiling=2 的证据从 2/3 变为 2/4。\n      加上 Pythia Code K*=1（已确认），Code domain 中 K*=1 的模型（Mistral + Pythia）\n      与 K*=2 的模型（Qwen-1.5B + LLaMA-8B）形成 2:2 split——无法建立 ceiling=2。\n\n  - name: \"Code Domain — Qwen-7B (RUNNING, worst-case prediction)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_code_qwen7b\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-7B Code/Python depth chain, predicted K*=1 or borderline\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 1\n      auc_0v1: [0.93, 0.96]\n      auc_1v2: [0.54, 0.60]\n      auc_2v3: [0.50, 0.54]\n      ci_1v2_upper: [0.58, 0.62]\n      note: \"CI may cross θ but point estimate below\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Qwen-7B 在 C4 上 1v2=0.6178（K*=2），但 Code domain 的 generation mode 不同：code\n      completion 比 web text continuation 更 constrained（syntax, indentation）。Qwen-7B\n      虽然有 code training data，但 code domain 的 structural regularity 加速 depth signal\n      消失。预期 AUC 1v2=0.54-0.60——point estimate 可能 < θ 或 borderline。如果 CI upper\n      恰好过 0.60 但 point estimate < 0.60，审稿人将判定 K*=1。Worst-case 下 Qwen-7B\n      Code 的 code competence 不足以在第二代文本中保留 distinguishable structure。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Qwen-7B C4 vs Code comparison\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Qwen-7B Code K*=1 使 Code domain 成为 2/5 K*=2（仅 Qwen-1.5B 和 LLaMA-8B），\n      直接触发 worst-case 的核心假设。Domain ceiling=2 退化为 \"two specific models happen\n      to achieve K*=2 on Code\"——不是 domain property 而是 model property。审稿人将\n      Code 和 C4 合并分析：C4 有 Mistral K*=1 exception，Code 有 Mistral+Qwen-7B+Pythia\n      K*=1——中间复杂度域的 K* 是 model-dependent 而非 domain-determined。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Additional RUNNING experiments\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Qwen-32B C4 (RUNNING, worst-case prediction)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_32b_c4\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-32B, C4 depth chain, worst-case prediction\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: [1, 2]\n      auc_0v1: [0.90, 0.94]\n      auc_1v2: [0.58, 0.62]\n      ci_1v2_lower: [0.57, 0.61]\n      note: \"borderline; may flip to K*=1\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      0v1 AUC declining trend with scale: 1.5B→0.997, 7B→0.9644, 14B→0.9598。\n      32B 预期 0v1 进一步下降至 0.90-0.94。1v2 AUC 趋势不明确（7B=0.6178, 14B=0.621,\n      scale 不单调），但 32B 生成的文本质量更高→depth signal 更弱。Worst-case 下 K*=1\n      或 borderline K*=2，进一步强化 \"K*=2 is a small-model phenomenon\" 的审稿人攻击线。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Scale trend 1.5B→7B→14B→32B\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"AUC vs scale trend plot with 32B prediction band\"\n    analysis: >\n      32B 结果如果 K*=1 或 borderline，审稿人将直接 extrapolate：\"at 70B+, K*=1 is\n      virtually certain. Your K*=2 finding is limited to ≤14B models and has no relevance\n      to the frontier models that dominate real-world text generation.\" 这是 scale\n      generalization concern 的 worst-case 实现。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Retrain Chain Extended (from registry, supporting C1')\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Qwen Retrain Chain Depth 7\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_qwen_retrain_depth7\"\n    description: \"Qwen-1.5B retrain chain extended to depth 7\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 7\n      auc_6v7: 0.641\n      ci_6v7_lower: 0.6376\n    result_rationale: >\n      Retrain K*=7 跨两个模型家族一致（Qwen 6v7=0.641, Pythia 6v7=0.634）——但 worst-case\n      下审稿人认为这完全是 LoRA artifact：\"7 rounds of LoRA fine-tuning accumulate vocabulary\n      narrowing and repetition bias that are trivially detectable. This has nothing to do\n      with text-intrinsic information loss.\" Retrain K*=7 vs prompt K*=2 的 3.5x 差距\n      进一步证明 K* is mechanism-dependent, not data-intrinsic。审稿人可能要求 full\n      fine-tuning（非 LoRA）来排除 adapter-specific artifacts——这在计算资源上不可行。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Retrain-chain pairwise AUC depth 0-7\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Prompt-chain vs retrain-chain K* divergence plot\"\n    analysis: >\n      Retrain depth 7 在 worst-case 下被完全 dismissed 为 \"LoRA artifact study\"。\n      论文将其定位为 \"upper bound\"，但审稿人质疑 \"an upper bound from a different mechanism\n      tells you nothing about the mechanism you claim to study (prompt-chain).\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Wikipedia Multi-Model (from registry, supporting C1')\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Wikipedia Scorer Confound Control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_wiki_scorer_confound + exp_wiki_scorer_confound_1b5\"\n    description: \"Cross-family scorer validation on Wikipedia\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star_after_control: 1\n      auc_1v2_cross_scorer: 0.587\n      delta_from_same_scorer: -0.024\n    result_rationale: >\n      Wiki scorer confound confirmed：same-family scorer inflates K* by +1（K*=2→1）。\n      Worst-case 下审稿人将此作为 systematic concern：\"if Wikipedia has a +1 scorer bias,\n      how do you know C4 doesn't have a similar bias? You only tested cross-scorer\n      on a subset of conditions.\" 论文承认 scorer confound 是 domain-specific，但审稿人\n      不接受 \"absence of evidence is not evidence of absence\"——C4 可能有未检测到的 bias。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Wiki same-scorer vs cross-scorer K*\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Wiki scorer confound 在 worst-case 下从 \"transparent disclosure\" 变为 \"systematic\n      methodology flaw\"。审稿人要求所有 domain×model 组合都做 cross-scorer validation\n      （total ~40 combos），论文仅完成 ~15，覆盖不足。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # arXiv Cross-Scorer (from registry, supporting C1')\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"arXiv Cross-Scorer Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_arXiv_qwen7b_crossscorer + others\"\n    description: \"arXiv cross-family scorer validation\"\n    expected_results:\n      qwen7b_crossscorer_k_star: 2\n      qwen7b_crossscorer_2v3: 0.5989\n      qwen1b5_crossscorer_k_star: 3\n      llama8b_crossscorer_k_star: 3\n      mistral7b_crossscorer_k_star: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      arXiv cross-scorer 揭示 Qwen-7B K*=3→2 drop（2v3=0.5989, just below θ）。\n      Worst-case 下审稿人指出 \"even arXiv K*=3 is not fully scorer-robust: one model\n      drops to K*=2 under cross-scoring. Cross-scorer preservation rate is 3/4=75%,\n      not 100%.\" 这落在 worst-case 指标范围 cross_scorer_kstar_preservation_rate=0.65-0.75\n      内。审稿人论证 arXiv 的 \"robust K*=3\" 也有 scorer confound 的 shadow。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: arXiv self-scorer vs cross-scorer comparison\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      arXiv cross-scorer 在 worst-case 下暴露 75% preservation rate（Qwen-7B drops），\n      比 C4 的 11/12=92% 低。如果 Code domain 也做 cross-scorer，preservation rate 预期\n      更低（worst-case 0.65-0.75）。审稿人总结：\"scorer independence is domain-dependent\n      and never fully holds, meaning K* is not purely text-intrinsic as claimed.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Code Domain Completed (from registry)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Code Domain — Qwen-1.5B\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_code_qwen1b5\"\n    description: \"Qwen-1.5B Code/Python depth chain\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 2\n      auc_0v1: 0.9388\n      auc_1v2: 0.7382\n      auc_2v3: 0.530\n      jsd_1v2: 0.0443\n      jsd_2v3: 0.0038\n    result_rationale: >\n      Qwen-1.5B Code K*=2 with strong margin（1v2=0.7382, +13.8pp above θ），JSD cliff\n      11.7x at 1v2→2v3。但 worst-case 下此 strong result 被 contextualized：(1) Qwen-1.5B\n      是 Qwen 家族的最小模型，其 code 能力有限→high 1v2 可能反映 \"poor code generation\n      easily detected\" 而非 domain property；(2) 仅 2/5 Code models 达到 K*=2，不足以\n      claim ceiling=2；(3) cross-scorer (Pythia) 确认 K*=2（0.7197）但 margin 下降 1.85pp。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Code domain model summary\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"JSD cliff comparison: Code vs C4 pattern difference\"\n    analysis: >\n      Qwen-1.5B Code K*=2 是 Code domain 最强的 data point，但 worst-case 下审稿人\n      将其与 Pythia K*=1 合并看：小模型在 Code 上 K*=1（Pythia）或 K*=2（Qwen），\n      取决于 code competence。如果 7B models 也 K*=1，则 Code ceiling=2 的证据 collapses。\n\n  - name: \"Code Domain — LLaMA-8B\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_code_llama8b\"\n    description: \"LLaMA-3.1-8B Code/Python depth chain\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 2\n      auc_0v1: 0.9161\n      auc_1v2: 0.7394\n      auc_2v3: 0.5112\n      jsd_1v2: 0.047\n      jsd_2v3: 0.0035\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLaMA Code K*=2 cross-family confirmed（1v2=0.7394, scored by Qwen）。但 worst-case\n      下审稿人注意到 2v3=0.5112 非常低（几乎 random），JSD cliff 13.5x。Code 的 K*=2\n      是 \"sharp cliff\"（1v2 很高但 2v3 几乎 chance），与 C4 的 gradual decline 不同。\n      审稿人可能认为 \"Code K*=2 simply means gen-1 code is detectable (trivially), but\n      by gen-2 it's already converged to generic code patterns.\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: LLaMA Code vs C4 comparison\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      LLaMA Code K*=2 提供 cross-family evidence，但 worst-case 下 sharp cliff pattern\n      被解读为 \"trivial gen-1 detection + immediate collapse\"——与 C4 的 more nuanced\n      depth signal 不同。审稿人可能质疑 Code 和 C4 是否真的 share ceiling=2 当 signal\n      dynamics 完全不同。\n\n  - name: \"Code Domain — Pythia-1.4B\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_code_pythia1b4\"\n    description: \"Pythia-1.4B Code/Python depth chain\"\n    expected_results:\n      k_star: 1\n      auc_0v1: 0.9592\n      auc_1v2: 0.5983\n      auc_2v3: 0.5215\n      note: \"fold-level 1v2 varies: 3/5 folds > 0.60 but aggregate mean < θ\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Pythia Code K*=1 reflects code generation competence 不足（The Pile 训练，code\n      占比低）。Worst-case 下审稿人直接引用：\"3 of 5 folds give 1v2 > 0.60 but the mean\n      is 0.5983 — your K* determination is literally a coin flip at the fold level.\n      θ=0.60 applied to means (not per-fold) is another methodological choice that\n      favors your narrative.\" 这加剧 θ cherry-picking 的指控。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Pythia Code per-fold breakdown\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Pythia Code K*=1 在 worst-case 下与 Mistral Code K*=1（predicted）合并，形成\n      \"3/5 Code models at K*=1\" 的局面，使 Code ceiling=2 claim 不可持续。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Paired Statistics (from registry, supporting C3)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Paired Statistical Tests for Filtering\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_E_paired_stats\"\n    description: \"Holm-Bonferroni corrected paired tests for C3\"\n    expected_results:\n      mmlu_significant_pairs: \"8/15\"\n      hellaswag_significant_pairs: \"9/15\"\n      binary_vs_all_mmlu: \"all significant\"\n      graduated_a09_vs_dsir_corrected_p: 0.0523\n    result_rationale: >\n      MMLU 仅 8/15 pairs significant after Holm-Bonferroni correction（bugfix 后从 10/15\n      降至 8/15）。Worst-case 下审稿人注意到 (1) graduated_a09 vs DSIR corrected p=0.0523\n      不显著——graduated filtering 甚至不能 beat DSIR；(2) binary wins but graduated ≈ DSIR\n      ≈ no_filter——depth-aware 的 graduated 方法完全没有优势；(3) Cohen's d 值很高（>8）\n      是因为 within-seed variance 极低，不代表 practically large effects。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Holm-Bonferroni corrected p-value matrix\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Statistical tests 在 worst-case 下支持 binary-ours significance 但彻底否定\n      graduated filtering。\"Binary outperforms\" 是 uninteresting（Drayson et al. already showed\n      this），\"graduated fails\" 是 C3 的 core negative result。高 Cohen's d + tiny absolute\n      delta = \"statistically significant, practically irrelevant\"。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Additional Plan Experiments\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"OBD vs Multiclass Comparison (n=500)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp_D_obd_n500\"\n    description: \"OBD accuracy vs LLM baselines with McNemar tests\"\n    expected_results:\n      obd_accuracy: 0.38\n      mcnemar_vs_gpt_p: 0.0809\n      mcnemar_vs_claude_p: 0.0693\n      mcnemar_significant: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      McNemar tests 不显著——OBD 与 frontier LLMs 在 5-class 上无显著差异。Worst-case 下\n      审稿人直接引用：\"your specialized 15-feature classifier does not significantly\n      outperform GPT-5.5 zero-shot on the task it was designed for.\" 这从 \"baseline\n      comparison\" 变为 \"our method is no better than prompting a frontier model.\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: OBD vs LLM McNemar results\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Non-significant McNemar 在 worst-case 下消除了 exp-011 的 positive framing。\n      审稿人看到 OBD=38% vs LLM=33%（p>0.05）会认为 \"no meaningful advantage from\n      specialized methodology — just use GPT.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Overall Worst-Case Summary\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Aggregate Worst-Case Assessment\"\n    plan_id: \"overall\"\n    description: \"Cross-experiment synthesis under worst-case scenario\"\n    expected_results:\n      domain_hierarchy_clean_fit: \"78-85%\"\n      code_ceiling2_support: \"2/5 models\"\n      c4_k2_at_theta060: \"8/9\"\n      c4_k2_at_theta065: \"~5/9\"\n      cross_scorer_preservation: \"65-75%\"\n      c3_validated_scope: \"Qwen-1.5B C4 binary only\"\n      c3_depth_aware_advantage: \"zero (graduated=no_filter everywhere)\"\n      estimated_reviewer_excitement: [2.8, 3.2]\n      emnlp_main_accept_prob: [0.05, 0.25]\n      emnlp_findings_prob: [0.30, 0.50]\n      aaai_with_70b_data_prob: [0.25, 0.40]\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst-case 的核心问题是 \"three-front attack\"：(1) K*≤3 trivial（审稿人不认为 bounded ≤3\n      是 surprising——\"of course models converge quickly, we knew that from model collapse\n      literature\"）；(2) C3 全面失败（graduated=no_filter, Pythia negative, arXiv negative）\n      → depth estimation 无 practical value；(3) θ=0.60 cherry-picking + scorer confound +\n      borderline CIs → K*=2 claim 的 statistical robustness 被质疑。三条线交汇时，审稿人\n      的 narrative 是 \"this paper measures something (K*) that is neither surprising (≤3)\n      nor useful (C3 fails) nor robust (θ-dependent), and the measurement methodology\n      (15D features) is standard text statistics.\" Reviewer excitement 2.8-3.2 对应\n      EMNLP \"Borderline Findings to Findings\" range——Main 几乎不可能（需要 4.0），Findings\n      需要 reframe 成功。\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Summary K* across all domains × models\"\n      - \"Table: C3 filtering results synthesis\"\n      - \"Table: θ-sensitivity summary\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grand summary: domain × model K* heatmap with worst-case Code columns\"\n      - \"Reviewer concern mapping to experimental evidence\"\n    analysis: >\n      Reframe 策略在 worst-case 下的可行性评估：\n      (A) Information-theoretic rapid convergence：最可行。放弃 \"domain ceiling\" 作为\n      predictive framework，转为 descriptive finding \"K*≤3 across all tested conditions\"。\n      DPI 理论保证有限但不给上界→实证 ≤3 是 non-trivial bound。但审稿人仍可能认为\n      model collapse 文献已 implicitly 知道这一点。需要 very strong writing 来 differentiate\n      \"first systematic measurement with operational definition\" vs \"known phenomenon,\n      just quantified.\"\n      (B) Measurement methodology：次可行。15D features 是 standard text statistics，\n      审稿人不认为方法论本身是贡献。除非 reframe 为 \"first reproducible protocol for\n      depth estimation\" with open-source toolkit——methodology paper 在 EMNLP Findings\n      有先例但 excitement 低。\n      最终评估：worst-case 下 EMNLP Main 接收概率 5-25%（需要至少一位 champion reviewer），\n      Findings 30-50%（如果 reframe 成功）。AAAI 2027 backup 有更多时间补充 70B+ 数据\n      和改进 C3（larger-scale filtering with full fine-tuning），但 AAAI 对 NLP-specific\n      methodology 的 appetite 较低。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"03f7a7fe-5346-4dc3-ab9a-d132249e2154","total_cost_usd":1.16234375,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":66913,"cache_read_input_tokens":145687,"output_tokens":24867,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":66913,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":24494,"cache_read_input_tokens":67451,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11303,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11303},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":49514,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.049599000000000004,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":24867,"cacheReadInputTokens":145687,"cacheCreationInputTokens":66913,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.11274475,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"2953f3e9-e859-44ec-a0d4-14a4477cd195"}
